var e={id:`australia`,name:`Australia`,flag:`🇦🇺`,currency:`AUD`,language:`English`,greeting:{text:`G'day`,meaning:`Hello (literally "good day")`},bestMonths:[3,4,5,9,10,11],tips:[`The UV index is extreme even on cloudy days: wear SPF 50+ sunscreen, a hat and sunglasses ("slip, slop, slap").`,`Only swim at patrolled beaches between the red-and-yellow flags; rips are strong and common.`,`In Sydney, tap a contactless card or phone on Opal readers for trains, buses, ferries and light rail. In Melbourne, use a myki card (or myki on Android); trams inside the CBD Free Tram Zone cost nothing.`,`Tipping is not expected because wages are high; rounding up or 10% for great restaurant service is appreciated.`,`Seasons are reversed: December–February is summer and June–August is winter. Most visitors need an ETA or eVisitor visa before arrival.`],cities:[{id:`sydney`,name:`Sydney`,lat:-33.8688,lng:151.2093,timezone:`Australia/Sydney`,tagline:`Harbour sparkle, golden beaches and the Opera House sails`,description:`Australia's biggest city wraps around one of the world's most beautiful harbours, with ferries as commuter transport and surf beaches minutes from downtown. Days revolve around the water, from Circular Quay to Bondi and Manly.`,idealDays:[3,5],places:[{id:`sydney-opera-house`,name:`Sydney Opera House`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`architecture`,`performance`,`unesco`,`rainy-day`],area:`Circular Quay`,lat:-33.8568,lng:151.2153,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:32,rating:5,description:`Jørn Utzon's sail-roofed masterpiece on Bennelong Point; take the one-hour guided tour by day or catch an opera, concert or show at night.`,tip:`Book tours and performances online in advance; at sunset the sails glow over the harbour, and a show is the best way to see the interiors.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Sydney Opera House`},{id:`opera-bar`,name:`Opera Bar`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bar`,`waterfront`,`sunset`,`night-view`,`live-music`],area:`Circular Quay`,lat:-33.8586,lng:151.2111,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`Outdoor drinks on the Opera House forecourt, with the Harbour Bridge lit up in front of you and live music most nights.`,tip:`Arrive before sunset on warm evenings to snag a waterfront table.`,indoor:!1},{id:`royal-botanic-garden`,name:`Royal Botanic Garden & Mrs Macquarie's Chair`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`gardens`,`viewpoint`,`sunset`,`kids`],area:`Circular Quay`,lat:-33.8642,lng:151.2166,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Harbourside gardens with sweeping lawns and native plants, leading to Mrs Macquarie's Chair, the classic viewpoint of the Opera House and Bridge together.`,tip:`Walk the foreshore from the Opera House to Mrs Macquarie's Chair for golden-hour photos.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Royal Botanic Garden, Sydney`},{id:`the-rocks`,name:`The Rocks`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`history`,`market`,`pubs`,`walk`],area:`The Rocks`,lat:-33.8599,lng:151.209,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Sydney's oldest quarter, a maze of sandstone laneways, convict-era buildings and historic pubs beneath the Harbour Bridge.`,tip:`The Rocks Markets run Saturdays and Sundays; finish with a beer at one of the pubs claiming to be Sydney's oldest.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`The Rocks, Sydney`},{id:`museum-of-contemporary-art`,name:`Museum of Contemporary Art Australia`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`art`,`rainy-day`,`rooftop`],area:`The Rocks`,lat:-33.86,lng:151.2088,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Free contemporary art on the edge of Circular Quay, with a strong collection of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander work.`,tip:`The rooftop café has one of the best-value Opera House views in the city.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museum of Contemporary Art Australia`},{id:`harbour-bridge-climb`,name:`Sydney Harbour BridgeClimb`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`iconic`,`viewpoint`,`adrenaline`,`sunset`],area:`The Rocks`,lat:-33.8523,lng:151.2108,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:210,rating:4,description:`Harnessed to the steel arch, climb 134 metres to the summit of the "Coathanger" for unbeatable 360-degree harbour views.`,tip:`Twilight climbs are the most popular and priciest; on a budget, walk the free bridge footpath or climb the Pylon Lookout instead.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Sydney Harbour Bridge`},{id:`art-gallery-of-nsw`,name:`Art Gallery of New South Wales`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`art`,`rainy-day`,`architecture`],area:`The Domain`,lat:-33.8688,lng:151.2173,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Australian, European, Asian and First Nations art across the original building and the striking SANAA-designed Naala Badu wing.`,tip:`General entry is free; on Wednesdays it stays open until 10pm with talks and music.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Art Gallery of New South Wales`},{id:`australian-museum`,name:`Australian Museum`,category:`family`,tags:[`free`,`kids`,`natural-history`,`dinosaurs`,`rainy-day`],area:`CBD`,lat:-33.8743,lng:151.2133,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Australia's oldest museum, with dinosaurs, native wildlife, minerals and First Nations galleries opposite Hyde Park.`,tip:`General admission is free; special exhibitions are ticketed.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Australian Museum`},{id:`queen-victoria-building`,name:`Queen Victoria Building`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`free`,`architecture`,`rainy-day`,`heritage`],area:`CBD`,lat:-33.8718,lng:151.2067,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A grand 1898 Romanesque arcade with stained glass, mosaic floors and ornate clocks, filled with boutiques and cafés.`,tip:`Look for the Great Australian Clock and the Royal Clock, which perform animated scenes on the hour.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Queen Victoria Building`},{id:`sea-life-sydney-aquarium`,name:`SEA LIFE Sydney Aquarium`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`aquarium`,`rainy-day`],area:`Darling Harbour`,lat:-33.8696,lng:151.2022,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:3,description:`Walk through underwater tunnels with sharks, dugongs and Great Barrier Reef fish on Darling Harbour.`,tip:`Buy online for a cheaper price, or bundle with WILD LIFE Sydney Zoo next door.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Sea Life Sydney Aquarium`},{id:`chinese-garden-of-friendship`,name:`Chinese Garden of Friendship`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`gardens`,`peaceful`,`tea`],area:`Darling Harbour`,lat:-33.8763,lng:151.2028,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:9,rating:3,description:`A tranquil walled garden of waterfalls, koi ponds and pavilions designed by Sydney's sister city Guangzhou.`,tip:`Stop for tea in the teahouse overlooking the lake.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Chinese Garden of Friendship`},{id:`sydney-fish-market`,name:`Sydney Fish Market`,category:`food`,tags:[`seafood`,`market`,`oysters`],area:`Pyrmont`,lat:-33.8726,lng:151.1916,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`The Southern Hemisphere's largest fish market, piled with fresh oysters, prawns and sashimi to eat on the waterfront.`,tip:`Arrive by late morning before the lunch rush and keep food covered from the bold seagulls.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Sydney Fish Market`},{id:`newtown`,name:`Newtown & King Street`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`street-art`,`live-music`,`vintage`,`food`],area:`Newtown`,lat:-33.897,lng:151.179,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:3,description:`Sydney's bohemian inner-west strip of street art, vintage shops, Thai restaurants, pubs and live-music venues.`,tip:`Take the train to Newtown station and wander the side streets for murals before dinner.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Newtown, New South Wales`},{id:`bondi-beach`,name:`Bondi Beach`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`iconic`,`free`,`beach`,`surf`,`kids`],area:`Bondi`,lat:-33.8915,lng:151.2767,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Australia's most famous crescent of golden sand and rolling surf, with the photogenic Icebergs ocean pool at its southern end.`,tip:`Swim between the red-and-yellow flags; a surf lesson is a great way to try the waves safely.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Bondi Beach`},{id:`bondi-to-coogee-walk`,name:`Bondi to Coogee Coastal Walk`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`hiking`,`coast`,`beaches`,`iconic`],area:`Bondi`,lat:-33.8951,lng:151.2744,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`A 6 km clifftop path linking Bondi, Tamarama, Bronte, Clovelly and Coogee beaches, with sandstone cliffs and ocean pools along the way.`,tip:`Start early to avoid the midday sun, bring swimmers for a dip, and catch a bus back from Coogee.`,indoor:!1},{id:`manly-ferry`,name:`Manly Ferry & Manly Beach`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`ferry`,`beach`,`viewpoint`,`iconic`],area:`Manly`,lat:-33.7969,lng:151.2887,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:4,description:`The 30-minute ferry from Circular Quay passes the Opera House and harbour headlands en route to Manly's surf beach and laid-back Corso.`,tip:`Tap on with Opal or a contactless card; sit outside on the left heading out for Opera House views.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Manly Beach`},{id:`taronga-zoo`,name:`Taronga Zoo`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`wildlife`,`koalas`,`viewpoint`,`ferry`],area:`Mosman`,lat:-33.8436,lng:151.2411,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:4,description:`Native animals from koalas to platypus, with giraffes grazing in front of a postcard skyline view across the harbour.`,tip:`Take the 12-minute ferry from Circular Quay, ride the Sky Safari cable car to the top entrance and walk downhill.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Taronga Zoo Sydney`},{id:`blue-mountains`,name:`Blue Mountains & Three Sisters`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`hiking`,`viewpoint`,`unesco`],area:`Blue Mountains`,lat:-33.732,lng:150.3119,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:5,description:`A UNESCO-listed plateau of eucalyptus-blue valleys and sandstone cliffs, with the Three Sisters rock formation at Echo Point in Katoomba.`,tip:`Take the train from Central to Katoomba (about 2 hours, cheap on Opal); Scenic World's railway and cableways cost extra. Leave early in summer.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Blue Mountains (Australia)`},{id:`barangaroo-reserve`,name:`Barangaroo Reserve`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`harbour-views`,`walking`,`sunset`],area:`Barangaroo`,lat:-33.8565,lng:151.2017,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A headland park rebuilt from sandstone blocks on a former container wharf, with native plantings and harbour views to the Harbour Bridge.`,tip:`Walk on along the Wulugul Walk waterfront to the restaurants and bars of Barangaroo South.`,indoor:!1},{id:`sydney-tower-eye`,name:`Sydney Tower Eye`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`night-view`,`rainy-day`],area:`CBD`,lat:-33.8705,lng:151.2089,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:3,description:`The observation deck of Sydney's tallest structure, with 360-degree views from the Blue Mountains to the Pacific.`,tip:`Tickets are cheaper online and often bundled with SEA LIFE and other Darling Harbour attractions.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Sydney Tower`},{id:`maritime-museum`,name:`Australian National Maritime Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`ships`,`history`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`Darling Harbour`,lat:-33.8691,lng:151.1985,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:4,description:`Galleries on seafaring Australia plus a fleet you can board, including a destroyer, a submarine and a full-size replica of Cook's Endeavour.`,tip:`General galleries are free; the ticket is only needed for the ships.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Australian National Maritime Museum`},{id:`hyde-park-barracks`,name:`Hyde Park Barracks`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`convicts`,`unesco`,`rainy-day`],area:`CBD`,lat:-33.8696,lng:151.2128,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:16,rating:4,description:`A UNESCO-listed 1819 convict barracks where an immersive audio tour tells the stories of the men who slept in its hammocks.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Hyde Park Barracks, Sydney`},{id:`watsons-bay`,name:`Watsons Bay & The Gap`,category:`nature`,tags:[`ferry`,`cliffs`,`seafood`,`sunset`],area:`Watsons Bay`,lat:-33.8433,lng:151.2817,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:4,description:`A village at the tip of South Head where calm harbour beaches meet dramatic Pacific sea cliffs a short walk away at The Gap.`,tip:`Ferry over from Circular Quay, walk the South Head track to Hornby Lighthouse, then eat fish and chips on the beach by Doyles.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Watsons Bay, New South Wales`},{id:`cockatoo-island`,name:`Cockatoo Island`,category:`culture`,tags:[`unesco`,`history`,`ferry`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Cockatoo Island`,lat:-33.8474,lng:151.1716,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:4,description:`A UNESCO-listed former convict prison and shipyard in the middle of the harbour, full of cavernous workshops, tunnels and gritty industrial relics.`,tip:`Grab an audio guide at the ferry wharf; you can even stay overnight in the waterfront campground.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Cockatoo Island (New South Wales)`},{id:`paddington`,name:`Paddington`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`neighbourhood`,`boutiques`,`galleries`,`terraces`],area:`Paddington`,lat:-33.8847,lng:151.2265,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Leafy streets of iron-laced Victorian terraces hiding designer boutiques, bookshops, galleries and cosy pubs.`,tip:`Come on a Saturday for the Paddington Markets in the Uniting Church grounds.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Paddington, New South Wales`},{id:`surry-hills`,name:`Surry Hills`,category:`food`,tags:[`neighbourhood`,`cafes`,`restaurants`,`brunch`],area:`Surry Hills`,lat:-33.8861,lng:151.2111,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`Sydney's dining heartland, where converted warehouses and terrace houses hold specialty coffee bars, brunch spots and some of the city's best restaurants.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Surry Hills, New South Wales`},{id:`bondi-icebergs`,name:`Bondi Icebergs Pool`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`swimming`,`ocean-pool`,`iconic`,`photography`],area:`Bondi`,lat:-33.8946,lng:151.2742,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:4,description:`The famous ocean pool at the south end of Bondi Beach, where waves crash over the edge of the lap lanes.`,tip:`The pool closes on Thursdays for cleaning; the bistro upstairs has the best views.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Bondi Icebergs Club`},{id:`luna-park-sydney`,name:`Luna Park Sydney`,category:`family`,tags:[`rides`,`kids`,`night-view`,`retro`],area:`Milsons Point`,lat:-33.8476,lng:151.21,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:3,description:`A 1935 harbourside amusement park entered through a giant grinning face, with vintage rides and Opera House views from the Ferris wheel.`,tip:`Entry is free; buy a ride pass online and check opening days, which vary outside school holidays.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Luna Park Sydney`},{id:`spit-to-manly-walk`,name:`Spit to Manly Walk`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`hiking`,`harbour-views`,`beaches`],area:`Mosman`,lat:-33.803,lng:151.2465,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A 10 km track through bushland, past Aboriginal rock engravings and secluded harbour beaches, finishing at the Manly Corso.`,tip:`Start at Spit Bridge so you finish in Manly and can catch the ferry back to Circular Quay.`,indoor:!1},{id:`carriageworks-farmers-market`,name:`Carriageworks Farmers Market`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`local`,`breakfast`,`weekend`],area:`Eveleigh`,lat:-33.8936,lng:151.1924,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`A Saturday-morning produce market in vast 19th-century railway workshops, packed with growers, bakers and breakfast stalls.`,tip:`Saturdays only, from early morning to early afternoon; Redfern station is a short walk away.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Carriageworks`},{id:`capitol-theatre`,name:`Capitol Theatre`,category:`culture`,tags:[`musicals`,`theatre`,`rainy-day`,`historic`],area:`Haymarket`,lat:-33.8806,lng:151.2063,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:90,rating:4,description:`A 1920s atmospheric theatre with a starlit ceiling that hosts Sydney's big touring musicals.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Capitol Theatre, Sydney`},{id:`chinatown-sydney`,name:`Chinatown`,category:`food`,tags:[`cheap-eats`,`night-market`,`asian-food`],area:`Haymarket`,lat:-33.879,lng:151.204,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`Dixon Street and its surrounding lanes buzz with yum cha halls, noodle bars, hot pot and late-night dessert shops.`,tip:`The Friday night market on Dixon Street adds street-food stalls.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Chinatown, Sydney`},{id:`palm-beach`,name:`Palm Beach & Barrenjoey Lighthouse`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`beach`,`lighthouse`,`viewpoint`],area:`Palm Beach`,lat:-33.596,lng:151.324,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`The glamorous tip of the Northern Beaches, with surf on one side, calm Pittwater on the other and a steep track up to a sandstone lighthouse.`,tip:`Buses run from the city but take well over an hour; driving the coast road is quicker. The lighthouse climb takes about 30 minutes.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Palm Beach, New South Wales`},{id:`royal-national-park`,name:`Royal National Park`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`hiking`,`beaches`,`wildlife`],area:`Royal National Park`,lat:-34.1373,lng:151.1167,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`The world's second-oldest national park, with sandstone cliffs, hidden beaches and a spectacular coastal track just south of the city.`,tip:`Go car-free by taking the train to Cronulla and the small ferry across to Bundeena.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Royal National Park`},{id:`wylies-baths`,name:`Wylie's Baths`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`ocean-pool`,`swimming`,`historic`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Coogee`,lat:-33.9104,lng:151.259,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:4,rating:4,description:`A 1907 tidal pool cut into the rocks at Coogee, with a timber boardwalk above clear water where fish swim alongside you.`,tip:`Bring snorkelling gear and come at low tide for the clearest water.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Wylie's Baths`},{id:`white-rabbit-gallery`,name:`White Rabbit Gallery`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`art`,`contemporary`,`rainy-day`],area:`Chippendale`,lat:-33.8858,lng:151.1975,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A free private gallery devoted to bold contemporary Chinese art, with a tea house serving dumplings on the ground floor.`,tip:`Opening days are limited (generally Wednesday to Sunday), so check before you go.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`White Rabbit Gallery`},{id:`sydney-observatory`,name:`Sydney Observatory`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`astronomy`,`history`,`views`],area:`The Rocks`,lat:-33.8597,lng:151.2045,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`An 1858 sandstone observatory on Observatory Hill, with free exhibits on astronomy and a grassy lawn looking out over the Harbour Bridge.`,tip:`Book a paid night-sky session to look through the historic telescopes.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Sydney Observatory`},{id:`oxford-street-darlinghurst`,name:`Oxford Street & Darlinghurst Bars`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`lgbtq`,`late-night`,`cocktails`],area:`Darlinghurst`,lat:-33.879,lng:151.218,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:3,description:`The heart of Sydney's LGBTQ+ scene and Mardi Gras parade route, lined with clubs, cocktail bars and late-night eateries.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Oxford Street, Sydney`}],foods:[{name:`Sydney rock oysters`,description:`Small, creamy, intensely briny native oysters, best freshly shucked with lemon.`},{name:`Fish and chips by the beach`,description:`Battered or grilled local fish with chips, eaten on the sand at Bondi, Manly or Watsons Bay.`},{name:`Smashed avo and a flat white`,description:`The Aussie café brunch: avocado on sourdough with feta or poached eggs, plus a velvety flat white.`},{name:`Meat pie`,description:`A handheld pie of minced beef and gravy; try a "Tiger" pie with mushy peas and mash at Harry's Café de Wheels.`},{name:`Pavlova`,description:`A crisp-shelled, marshmallowy meringue topped with cream and fresh fruit such as passionfruit.`},{name:`Lamington`,description:`Squares of sponge cake dipped in chocolate and rolled in desiccated coconut.`}]},{id:`melbourne`,name:`Melbourne`,lat:-37.8136,lng:144.9631,timezone:`Australia/Melbourne`,tagline:`Laneway coffee, street art and four seasons in a day`,description:`Australia's cultural capital rewards wandering: hidden laneways, world-class coffee, galleries, sport-obsessed crowds and a superb multicultural food scene. Its free CBD trams make it easy to explore, and great day trips reach the coast and wildlife.`,idealDays:[3,5],places:[{id:`federation-square`,name:`Federation Square`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`architecture`,`events`,`meeting-point`],area:`CBD`,lat:-37.818,lng:144.9691,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Melbourne's angular, much-debated civic square opposite Flinders Street Station, hosting free events, screens and galleries.`,tip:`Start here at the visitor hub, then cross to the grand Flinders Street Station clocks for a classic photo.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Federation Square`},{id:`acmi`,name:`ACMI (Australian Centre for the Moving Image)`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`film`,`games`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`CBD`,lat:-37.8176,lng:144.969,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A free, highly interactive museum of film, TV and video games inside Federation Square.`,tip:`Grab a Lens at the entrance to "collect" exhibits and explore them later online.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Australian Centre for the Moving Image`},{id:`hosier-lane`,name:`Hosier Lane`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`street-art`,`photo`,`laneways`,`iconic`],area:`CBD`,lat:-37.8164,lng:144.9692,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A cobbled laneway layered floor to roof with constantly changing graffiti and street art.`,tip:`Continue into neighbouring AC/DC Lane and Duckboard Place for more murals with fewer crowds.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hosier Lane`},{id:`degraves-street`,name:`Degraves Street & Centre Place`,category:`food`,tags:[`coffee`,`laneways`,`cafes`,`iconic`],area:`CBD`,lat:-37.8168,lng:144.9655,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`Narrow, buzzing laneways packed with tiny cafés and outdoor tables, the essence of Melbourne's coffee culture.`,tip:`Order a flat white standing up like the locals, then explore the Block Arcade and Royal Arcade nearby.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Degraves Street`},{id:`city-circle-tram`,name:`City Circle Tram`,category:`family`,tags:[`free`,`transport`,`heritage`,`kids`],area:`CBD`,lat:-37.8183,lng:144.9671,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Free heritage trams loop around the CBD and Docklands with audio commentary on city landmarks.`,tip:`Hop on and off anywhere along the loop; any tram within the Free Tram Zone is also free, no myki needed.`,indoor:!1},{id:`rooftop-bar-curtin-house`,name:`Rooftop Bar (Curtin House)`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`rooftop`,`bar`,`cinema`,`night-view`],area:`CBD`,lat:-37.8117,lng:144.9661,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:3,description:`A laid-back rooftop bar seven floors above Swanston Street, home to the Rooftop Cinema on summer nights.`,tip:`Rooftop Cinema runs roughly December to April; book film tickets ahead and bring a layer for cool evenings.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Curtin House`},{id:`queen-victoria-market`,name:`Queen Victoria Market`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`market`,`food`,`souvenirs`,`heritage`],area:`CBD`,lat:-37.8076,lng:144.9568,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`A sprawling 19th-century open-air market of fresh produce, delis, souvenirs and hot food stalls.`,tip:`Closed Mondays and Wednesdays; don't miss the hot jam doughnuts from the American Doughnut Kitchen van. Wednesday night markets run in summer.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Queen Victoria Market`},{id:`eureka-skydeck`,name:`Melbourne Skydeck`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`night-view`,`sunset`,`rainy-day`],area:`Southbank`,lat:-37.8214,lng:144.9645,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:3,description:`The 88th-floor observation deck of Eureka Tower, with views to the bay and the Dandenongs and a glass cube that slides out over the edge.`,tip:`Go around sunset to see the city lights come on; The Edge glass cube costs extra.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Eureka Tower`},{id:`ngv-international`,name:`National Gallery of Victoria (NGV International)`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`art`,`rainy-day`,`iconic`],area:`Southbank`,lat:-37.8226,lng:144.9689,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Australia's oldest and most-visited gallery, entered through a famous water wall and crowned by a stained-glass ceiling in the Great Hall.`,tip:`The permanent collection is free; lie on the Great Hall carpet to admire the ceiling. Australian art is across the river at the Ian Potter Centre in Federation Square.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National Gallery of Victoria`},{id:`royal-botanic-gardens`,name:`Royal Botanic Gardens Melbourne`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`gardens`,`picnic`,`kids`],area:`Kings Domain`,lat:-37.8304,lng:144.9796,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Thirty-eight hectares of lawns, lakes and plant collections beside the Yarra, with a dedicated children's garden.`,tip:`Combine with the Shrine of Remembrance next door; the Ian Potter Children's Garden closes for maintenance in mid-winter.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Royal Botanic Gardens, Melbourne`},{id:`shrine-of-remembrance`,name:`Shrine of Remembrance`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`history`,`viewpoint`,`memorial`,`rainy-day`],area:`Kings Domain`,lat:-37.8305,lng:144.9734,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A monumental war memorial with moving galleries beneath and a balcony looking straight up St Kilda Road to the skyline.`,tip:`At 11am a ray of light falls on the Stone of Remembrance in the sanctuary, recreated hourly with a mirror.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Shrine of Remembrance`},{id:`melbourne-cricket-ground`,name:`Melbourne Cricket Ground (MCG)`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`sport`,`iconic`,`tour`,`afl`,`cricket`],area:`Yarra Park`,lat:-37.82,lng:144.9834,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`The 100,000-seat "G" is a temple of Australian sport; tour the stands and the Australian Sports Museum, or join the roar of an AFL or cricket crowd.`,tip:`AFL season runs March to September and cricket in summer; a live match beats the tour for atmosphere.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Melbourne Cricket Ground`},{id:`melbourne-museum`,name:`Melbourne Museum & Royal Exhibition Building`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`natural-history`,`unesco`,`rainy-day`],area:`Carlton`,lat:-37.8033,lng:144.9717,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:11,rating:4,description:`Dinosaurs, a living forest gallery and the excellent Bunjilaka Aboriginal Cultural Centre, beside the UNESCO-listed 1880 Royal Exhibition Building.`,tip:`Children enter free; book a guided tour to see inside the Royal Exhibition Building.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Melbourne Museum`},{id:`lygon-street`,name:`Lygon Street`,category:`food`,tags:[`italian`,`gelato`,`coffee`,`dinner`],area:`Carlton`,lat:-37.7985,lng:144.967,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:3,description:`Melbourne's "Little Italy", lined with trattorias, espresso bars and gelaterias since post-war migration.`,tip:`Skip the restaurants with spruikers out front and look for long-standing spots like Brunetti for cannoli and coffee.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lygon Street`},{id:`fitzroy`,name:`Fitzroy & Brunswick Street`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`vintage`,`bars`,`street-art`,`live-music`,`cafes`],area:`Fitzroy`,lat:-37.799,lng:144.9784,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Melbourne's creative hub of vintage stores, record shops, street art, cafés and buzzing bars that stay lively late.`,tip:`Take tram 11 up Brunswick St, then wander Gertrude and Smith Streets for design shops and dinner.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Fitzroy, Victoria`},{id:`st-kilda`,name:`St Kilda Beach & Pier`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`free`,`beach`,`sunset`,`penguins`,`kids`],area:`St Kilda`,lat:-37.8636,lng:144.9741,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A palm-lined bayside suburb with a long pier, retro Luna Park and Acland Street cake shops; little penguins return to the breakwater at dusk.`,tip:`Penguin viewing is free but follow volunteer guidance and never use flash; take tram 96 from the CBD.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`St Kilda, Victoria`},{id:`phillip-island-penguin-parade`,name:`Phillip Island Penguin Parade`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`wildlife`,`penguins`,`kids`,`iconic`],area:`Phillip Island`,lat:-38.5101,lng:145.149,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:5,description:`At sunset, hundreds of little penguins waddle ashore across Summerland Beach to their burrows, a magical wildlife spectacle.`,tip:`It is about 2 hours' drive each way; book tickets ahead, bring warm clothes year-round, and note photography of the penguins is banned. Organised tours from Melbourne cost around US$100+.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Phillip Island`},{id:`great-ocean-road`,name:`Great Ocean Road & Twelve Apostles`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`day-trip`,`road-trip`,`coast`,`viewpoint`,`iconic`],area:`Great Ocean Road`,lat:-38.6655,lng:143.105,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:100,rating:5,description:`One of the world's great coastal drives, past surf towns and rainforest to the towering limestone stacks of the Twelve Apostles.`,tip:`As a day trip it is a long 12+ hour round trip; take a tour or, better, stay overnight in Lorne or Apollo Bay. Drive on the left and watch for wildlife at dusk.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Great Ocean Road`},{id:`state-library-victoria`,name:`State Library Victoria`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`architecture`,`rainy-day`,`library`],area:`CBD`,lat:-37.8098,lng:144.9652,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A grand 19th-century library whose octagonal La Trobe Reading Room rises to a soaring domed skylight.`,tip:`Climb to the upper galleries of the dome for the best view of the reading room.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`State Library Victoria`},{id:`block-arcade`,name:`The Block Arcade`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`architecture`,`arcade`,`afternoon-tea`,`rainy-day`],area:`CBD`,lat:-37.8155,lng:144.9646,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`An ornate 1892 shopping arcade with mosaic floors and a glass canopy, home to the gilded Hopetoun Tea Rooms.`,tip:`The cake-filled window at Hopetoun Tea Rooms draws a queue; come early or settle for a takeaway slice.`,indoor:!0},{id:`chinatown-melbourne`,name:`Chinatown`,category:`food`,tags:[`cheap-eats`,`dumplings`,`late-night`,`history`],area:`CBD`,lat:-37.8115,lng:144.969,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`The western world's longest continuous Chinatown, a red-arched stretch of Little Bourke Street packed with dumpling houses and late-night restaurants.`,tip:`The Museum of Chinese Australian History on Cohen Place tells the gold-rush backstory.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Chinatown, Melbourne`},{id:`arts-centre-melbourne`,name:`Arts Centre Melbourne`,category:`culture`,tags:[`theatre`,`ballet`,`opera`,`rainy-day`],area:`Southbank`,lat:-37.8213,lng:144.9688,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:70,rating:4,description:`Melbourne's performing-arts hub under a lacy illuminated spire, staging opera, ballet and musicals, with the Melbourne Symphony Orchestra next door at Hamer Hall.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Arts Centre Melbourne`},{id:`south-melbourne-market`,name:`South Melbourne Market`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`local`,`dim-sims`,`rainy-day`],area:`South Melbourne`,lat:-37.8326,lng:144.9562,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`A friendly local market famous for its steamed dim sims, fresh oysters and a maze of produce, deli and homewares stalls.`,tip:`Open Wednesday and Friday to Sunday only; the dim sim stall queues are worth it.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`South Melbourne Market`},{id:`chapel-street`,name:`Chapel Street`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`fashion`,`boutiques`,`bars`,`neighbourhood`],area:`South Yarra`,lat:-37.846,lng:144.993,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A long, buzzing strip of fashion boutiques, vintage shops, cafés and bars running through South Yarra, Prahran and Windsor.`,tip:`Duck into Prahran Market just off Chapel Street for gourmet snacks.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Chapel Street, Melbourne`},{id:`brighton-bathing-boxes`,name:`Brighton Bathing Boxes`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`beach`,`photography`,`colourful`],area:`Brighton`,lat:-37.9165,lng:144.9867,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A row of 82 brightly painted beach huts on Dendy Street Beach, with the city skyline across the bay.`,tip:`Take the Sandringham train to Brighton Beach station and walk south along the foreshore.`,indoor:!1},{id:`melbourne-zoo`,name:`Melbourne Zoo`,category:`family`,tags:[`zoo`,`animals`,`kids`,`native-wildlife`],area:`Parkville`,lat:-37.7841,lng:144.9515,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`Australia's oldest zoo, with a lush gorilla rainforest, elephants and native animals including platypus and koalas.`,tip:`Children under 16 enter free on weekends and Victorian school holidays.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Melbourne Zoo`},{id:`immigration-museum`,name:`Immigration Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`rainy-day`,`migration`],area:`CBD`,lat:-37.8192,lng:144.9605,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`Personal stories of the people who built multicultural Melbourne, displayed in the grand 1876 Old Customs House by the Yarra.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Immigration Museum, Melbourne`},{id:`old-melbourne-gaol`,name:`Old Melbourne Gaol`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`spooky`,`bushrangers`,`rainy-day`],area:`CBD`,lat:-37.8078,lng:144.9653,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`A bluestone 1840s prison where Ned Kelly was hanged, with tiny cells, death masks and a mock arrest in the old City Watch House.`,tip:`Evening ghost and hangman tours run on select nights for a spookier visit.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Old Melbourne Gaol`},{id:`abbotsford-convent`,name:`Abbotsford Convent`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`arts`,`gardens`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Abbotsford`,lat:-37.8025,lng:145.0045,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A heritage convent on the Yarra converted into artist studios, galleries, cafés and gardens, next to the Collingwood Children's Farm.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Abbotsford Convent`},{id:`yarra-valley`,name:`Yarra Valley Wineries`,category:`food`,tags:[`day-trip`,`wine`,`tasting`,`scenic`],area:`Yarra Valley`,lat:-37.68,lng:145.43,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:120,rating:4,description:`Rolling vineyards an hour from the city, famous for sparkling wine, pinot noir and cellar-door lunches, with Healesville Sanctuary's native wildlife nearby.`,tip:`Book a winery tour so nobody has to drive.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Yarra Valley`},{id:`puffing-billy`,name:`Puffing Billy Railway`,category:`family`,tags:[`steam-train`,`kids`,`forest`,`half-day`],area:`Dandenong Ranges`,lat:-37.9095,lng:145.354,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`A century-old steam train chugging through the fern gullies of the Dandenong Ranges, with passengers dangling their legs out of the open carriages.`,tip:`Take the metro train to Belgrave, a short walk from the station; book weekend and holiday trips in advance.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Puffing Billy Railway`},{id:`peninsula-hot-springs`,name:`Peninsula Hot Springs`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`spa`,`thermal-baths`,`day-trip`,`sunset`],area:`Mornington Peninsula`,lat:-38.414,lng:144.867,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:70,rating:4,description:`Natural geothermal pools set among the dunes of the Mornington Peninsula, topped by a hilltop pool with sweeping views.`,tip:`Book Bath House entry ahead, especially on weekends.`,indoor:!1},{id:`corner-hotel`,name:`Corner Hotel`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`live-music`,`rooftop`,`pub`,`rainy-day`],area:`Richmond`,lat:-37.8252,lng:144.9918,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:4,description:`A beloved Richmond pub and band room that has hosted local and touring acts for decades, with a rooftop bar overlooking Swan Street.`,indoor:!0},{id:`fitzroy-gardens`,name:`Fitzroy Gardens`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`gardens`,`history`,`walking`],area:`East Melbourne`,lat:-37.8131,lng:144.9798,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Elm-lined Victorian gardens at the city's edge with a conservatory, a fairy tree and Captain Cook's Cottage, shipped from England in 1934.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Fitzroy Gardens`},{id:`sea-life-melbourne`,name:`SEA LIFE Melbourne Aquarium`,category:`family`,tags:[`aquarium`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`penguins`],area:`CBD`,lat:-37.8208,lng:144.9584,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:32,rating:3,description:`An aquarium on the Yarra with a shark-filled oceanarium, a walk-through tunnel and a sub-Antarctic penguin colony.`,tip:`Tickets are cheaper online and in combos with the Skydeck.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Sea Life Melbourne Aquarium`},{id:`pellegrinis`,name:`Pellegrini's Espresso Bar`,category:`food`,tags:[`coffee`,`italian`,`retro`,`iconic`],area:`CBD`,lat:-37.8113,lng:144.9712,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`A 1954 espresso bar that helped bring coffee culture to Melbourne, unchanged down to the chequered floor, counter stools and hearty pasta.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Pellegrini's Espresso Bar`},{id:`albert-park-lake`,name:`Albert Park Lake`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`walking`,`running`,`skyline`],area:`Albert Park`,lat:-37.8455,lng:144.971,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A lake ringed by a 5 km running path with black swans and city views, which becomes the Australian Grand Prix circuit each autumn.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Albert Park and Lake`},{id:`luna-park-melbourne`,name:`Luna Park Melbourne`,category:`family`,tags:[`rides`,`kids`,`retro`,`iconic`],area:`St Kilda`,lat:-37.8679,lng:144.9766,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:3,description:`A 1912 seaside amusement park behind a giant laughing mouth, home to the Scenic Railway, the world's oldest continuously operating roller coaster.`,tip:`Opening days and hours vary by season; check ahead and buy an unlimited-ride pass online.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Luna Park Melbourne`}],foods:[{name:`Flat white`,description:`A strong, velvety espresso with microfoam milk, perfected in Melbourne's obsessive café culture.`},{name:`Hot jam doughnuts`,description:`Piping-hot sugared doughnuts filled with jam from the van at Queen Victoria Market, a tradition since 1950.`},{name:`Chicken parma`,description:`The pub classic: crumbed chicken schnitzel topped with napoli sauce, ham and melted cheese, served with chips and salad.`},{name:`Souvlaki`,description:`Melbourne has one of the world's largest Greek communities; grab a lamb souva wrapped in pita.`},{name:`Dim sims`,description:`A Melbourne-invented, oversized steamed or fried dumpling, best known from South Melbourne Market.`},{name:`Laneway brunch`,description:`Inventive café brunches, from smashed avo to ricotta hotcakes, in converted warehouses and tiny laneway spots.`}]},{id:`brisbane`,name:`Brisbane`,lat:-27.46778,lng:153.02806,timezone:`Australia/Brisbane`,tagline:`Subtropical river city, koalas and beaches either side`,description:`Queensland's sunny, easygoing capital wraps around a winding river crossed by fast CityCat ferries. Free riverside parklands, a strong gallery precinct and a lively night scene fill the city days, while the Gold Coast, Sunshine Coast hinterland and sand islands of Moreton Bay are all within easy day-trip reach.`,idealDays:[3,6],places:[{id:`south-bank-parklands`,name:`South Bank Parklands`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`riverside`,`parkland`,`iconic`,`walking`],area:`South Bank`,lat:-27.4787,lng:153.0229,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`A long riverside strip of lawns, rainforest walks, bougainvillea-covered arbour and cafés facing the city skyline, the heart of Brisbane's outdoor life.`,tip:`Walk the Grand Arbour at dusk, then cross the Goodwill Bridge for city lights over the water.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`South Bank Parklands`},{id:`streets-beach`,name:`Streets Beach`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`free`,`swimming`,`lagoon`,`kids`,`summer`],area:`South Bank`,lat:-27.47826,lng:153.0236,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A free, lifeguard-patrolled man-made lagoon with real sand and palm trees, right beside the river in the middle of the city.`,tip:`Bring swimmers and sunscreen; it is busiest on summer weekend afternoons, so go early.`,indoor:!1},{id:`gallery-of-modern-art`,name:`Gallery of Modern Art (GOMA)`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`art`,`contemporary`,`rainy-day`,`architecture`],area:`South Bank (Cultural Centre)`,lat:-27.47061,lng:153.01723,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Australia's largest modern art gallery, with big, playful contemporary and Asia-Pacific collections in a light-filled riverside building.`,tip:`The older Queensland Art Gallery next door is part of the same free complex and has a calm water mall to rest by.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Gallery of Modern Art, Brisbane`},{id:`queensland-museum`,name:`Queensland Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`natural-history`,`dinosaurs`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`South Bank (Cultural Centre)`,lat:-27.47341,lng:153.01842,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The state museum of natural and cultural history, from Queensland dinosaurs and Great Barrier Reef wildlife to First Nations collections.`,tip:`General entry is free; the hands-on SparkLab science centre inside charges a small fee and suits kids.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Queensland Museum`},{id:`queensland-performing-arts-centre`,name:`Queensland Performing Arts Centre (QPAC)`,category:`culture`,tags:[`theatre`,`music`,`ballet`,`shows`,`night`],area:`South Bank (Cultural Centre)`,lat:-27.475,lng:153.02,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:70,rating:3,description:`Brisbane's main performing arts venue, hosting touring musicals, the Queensland Symphony Orchestra, ballet and opera across several theatres.`,tip:`Check the programme before you travel; big musicals sell out, but rush and restricted-view seats can be good value.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Queensland Performing Arts Centre`},{id:`wheel-of-brisbane`,name:`Wheel of Brisbane`,category:`family`,tags:[`views`,`observation-wheel`,`kids`,`night`],area:`South Bank`,lat:-27.47532,lng:153.02086,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:15,rating:2,description:`A 60-metre observation wheel with enclosed, air-conditioned gondolas giving a slow loop of views over the river and skyline.`,tip:`Ride after dark when the city and bridges are lit up.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Wheel of Brisbane`},{id:`queens-wharf`,name:`Queen's Wharf & Neville Bonner Bridge`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`views`,`riverside`,`bars`,`new`,`night`],area:`CBD (George Street)`,lat:-27.47423,lng:153.02521,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A new riverside precinct of restored heritage buildings, restaurants, bars and an elevated Sky Deck, linked to South Bank by a pedestrian bridge.`,tip:`Walk over the Neville Bonner Bridge from South Bank at sunset, then head up to the Sky Deck for the view.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Queen's Wharf, Brisbane`},{id:`museum-of-brisbane`,name:`Museum of Brisbane & City Hall Clock Tower`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`history`,`heritage`,`views`,`rainy-day`],area:`CBD (King George Square)`,lat:-27.46876,lng:153.02347,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A free museum about the city's people and stories inside grand 1930 City Hall, with tours up the old clock tower in a vintage cage lift.`,tip:`The free clock tower tours are short and limited in number; book a time slot at the museum desk when you arrive.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museum of Brisbane`},{id:`queen-street-mall`,name:`Queen Street Mall`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`free`,`shopping`,`arcades`,`street-performers`],area:`CBD`,lat:-27.4696,lng:153.0252,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The city's pedestrian shopping spine, lined with department stores, arcades and buskers between Edward and George streets.`,tip:`Duck into the heritage Brisbane Arcade for boutiques and old-world shopfronts.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Queen Street Mall`},{id:`city-botanic-gardens`,name:`City Botanic Gardens`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`gardens`,`riverside`,`walking`,`picnic`],area:`CBD (Gardens Point)`,lat:-27.4747,lng:153.0301,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Queensland's oldest public gardens, with shady fig avenues, bamboo groves and a mangrove boardwalk along the river edge.`,tip:`Follow the mangrove boardwalk at high tide, then continue to the Kangaroo Point Cliffs view across the water.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Brisbane City Botanic Gardens`},{id:`commissariat-store`,name:`Commissariat Store Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`heritage`,`convict`,`small`],area:`CBD (William Street)`,lat:-27.4732,lng:153.0242,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:2,description:`A convict-built 1829 stone storehouse, one of the oldest buildings in Queensland, now a small museum of the colony's early years.`,tip:`Opening days are limited, usually midweek; check hours before you go.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Commissariat Store, Brisbane`},{id:`st-johns-cathedral`,name:`St John's Cathedral`,category:`culture`,tags:[`free`,`architecture`,`gothic`,`quiet`],area:`CBD (Ann Street)`,lat:-27.46398,lng:153.03006,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A soaring Gothic Revival cathedral with a stone-vaulted ceiling, built in stages over more than a century and finished only in 2009.`,tip:`Look up at the carved stone vaulting, rare in Australia; volunteers often offer free guided walks.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`St John's Cathedral (Brisbane)`},{id:`citycat-ferry`,name:`CityCat Ferry Ride`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`river`,`ferry`,`cheap`,`views`,`iconic`],area:`Brisbane River`,lat:-27.46325,lng:153.03754,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:.5,rating:5,description:`Fast catamaran ferries that zigzag the Brisbane River from the University of Queensland to Northshore Hamilton, the best and cheapest city tour.`,tip:`Public transport fares in Queensland are a flat 50 cents; ride end to end and sit outside at the back.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`RiverCity Ferries`},{id:`story-bridge-adventure-climb`,name:`Story Bridge Adventure Climb`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`climb`,`views`,`bridge`,`sunset`,`bucket-list`],area:`Kangaroo Point`,lat:-27.4678,lng:153.03564,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:100,rating:4,description:`A guided, harnessed climb to the top of Brisbane's 1940 steel cantilever bridge, 80 metres above the river.`,tip:`Twilight climbs sell out first; you can also walk the bridge footpath for free.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Story Bridge`},{id:`kangaroo-point-cliffs`,name:`Kangaroo Point Cliffs`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`free`,`views`,`rock-climbing`,`abseiling`,`sunset`],area:`Kangaroo Point`,lat:-27.47838,lng:153.03408,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Floodlit volcanic cliffs above the river, popular for climbing and abseiling and for one of the best free skyline views in town.`,tip:`Come at sunset with takeaway and sit on the clifftop lawns; guided climbing and abseiling sessions run here too.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Kangaroo Point Cliffs`},{id:`howard-smith-wharves`,name:`Howard Smith Wharves`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`brewery`,`riverside`,`dining`,`night`],area:`CBD (under the Story Bridge)`,lat:-27.46313,lng:153.03824,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`Restored riverside wharves beneath the Story Bridge, now packed with a brewery, bars and restaurants that fill up on warm evenings.`,tip:`Arrive by CityCat; the Felons brewery beer hall is the easiest walk-in spot.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Howard Smith Wharves`},{id:`fortitude-valley`,name:`Fortitude Valley`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`live-music`,`clubs`,`night`,`laneways`],area:`Fortitude Valley`,lat:-27.4566,lng:153.0372,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:3,description:`Brisbane's nightlife hub of live-music venues, rooftop bars and clubs, with Chinatown and the chic James Street shopping strip close by.`,tip:`Brunswick Street Mall is the centre; the Brisbane Jazz Club near the river is a calmer alternative.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Fortitude Valley`},{id:`brisbane-powerhouse`,name:`Brisbane Powerhouse`,category:`culture`,tags:[`arts`,`comedy`,`markets`,`riverside`,`night`],area:`New Farm`,lat:-27.46907,lng:153.05436,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`A graffiti-marked former power station turned arts centre, staging comedy, theatre and live music beside New Farm Park.`,tip:`The Jan Powers farmers market fills the grounds on Saturday mornings.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Brisbane Powerhouse`},{id:`new-farm-park`,name:`New Farm Park`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`free`,`park`,`picnic`,`jacarandas`,`riverside`],area:`New Farm`,lat:-27.4692,lng:153.0512,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A big riverside park with rose gardens, huge fig trees and picnic lawns, loved by locals on weekends.`,tip:`In late October and November the park's jacarandas turn purple; walk back to the city on the New Farm Riverwalk.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`New Farm Park`},{id:`roma-street-parkland`,name:`Roma Street Parkland`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`gardens`,`walking`,`picnic`],area:`CBD (Spring Hill)`,lat:-27.463,lng:153.019,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A large landscaped garden in the city with a subtropical rainforest walk, lake and colourful seasonal displays.`,tip:`It sits next to Roma Street station, handy for a stroll on arrival or before an airport train.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Roma Street Parkland`},{id:`queensland-maritime-museum`,name:`Queensland Maritime Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`ships`,`kids`,`riverside`],area:`South Bank`,lat:-27.48194,lng:153.02611,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:2,description:`A volunteer-run museum in a historic dry dock, where you can board the Second World War frigate HMAS Diamantina.`,tip:`Open Wednesday to Sunday only, with last entry an hour before closing.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Queensland Maritime Museum`},{id:`west-end`,name:`West End`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`markets`,`bohemian`,`cafes`,`vintage`,`street-art`],area:`West End`,lat:-27.483,lng:153.0066,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A bohemian inner suburb of vintage shops, cafés and multicultural eateries, best on Saturday for the Davies Park market.`,tip:`The Saturday morning market at Davies Park runs under giant fig trees with food stalls and local produce.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`West End, Queensland`},{id:`xxxx-brewery-tour`,name:`XXXX Brewery Tour`,category:`food`,tags:[`beer`,`brewery`,`tour`,`tasting`],area:`Milton`,lat:-27.46697,lng:153.00518,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:28,rating:3,description:`A guided tour of the Milton brewery that has made Queensland's best-known beer for well over a century, ending with tastings in the Alehouse.`,tip:`Book ahead, bring photo ID and wear closed flat shoes; there are many stairs on the route.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Castlemaine Perkins`},{id:`eat-street-northshore`,name:`Eat Street Northshore`,category:`food`,tags:[`street-food`,`night-market`,`live-music`,`containers`],area:`Hamilton`,lat:-27.44415,lng:153.08025,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`A weekend night market built from shipping containers on the river at Hamilton, with dozens of food stalls, bars and live music.`,tip:`Open Friday to Sunday from late afternoon; there is a small entry fee, and the CityCat stops at Northshore Hamilton.`,indoor:!1},{id:`lone-pine-koala-sanctuary`,name:`Lone Pine Koala Sanctuary`,category:`family`,tags:[`koalas`,`wildlife`,`kangaroos`,`kids`,`iconic`],area:`Fig Tree Pocket`,lat:-27.53293,lng:152.9693,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:5,description:`The world's first and largest koala sanctuary, where you can hand-feed free-roaming kangaroos and see more than 100 koalas.`,tip:`Arrive by the Mirimar river cruise from the city for a scenic trip there; koalas are most active in the morning.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lone Pine Koala Sanctuary`},{id:`mount-coot-tha-lookout`,name:`Mount Coot-tha Lookout`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`views`,`sunset`,`bushwalking`],area:`Mount Coot-tha`,lat:-27.48501,lng:152.95895,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The city's highest lookout, with sweeping views over the skyline, river and out to Moreton Bay on a clear day.`,tip:`Go for sunset; bus 471 runs up from the city, and bush trails lead down to the Botanic Gardens.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Mount Coot-tha`},{id:`brisbane-botanic-gardens-mount-coot-tha`,name:`Brisbane Botanic Gardens, Mount Coot-tha`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`gardens`,`japanese-garden`,`rainforest`],area:`Mount Coot-tha`,lat:-27.4765,lng:152.9761,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Expansive subtropical gardens with a Japanese garden, tropical display dome and arid and rainforest collections.`,tip:`Pair it with the Mount Coot-tha Lookout on the same afternoon.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Brisbane Botanic Gardens, Mount Coot-tha`},{id:`north-stradbroke-island`,name:`North Stradbroke Island (Point Lookout)`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`island`,`beaches`,`whales`,`wildlife`],area:`Minjerribah (Moreton Bay)`,lat:-27.4297,lng:153.54,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:5,description:`A big sand island reached by ferry from Cleveland, with surf beaches and the North Gorge headland walk where turtles, dolphins and whales are often seen.`,tip:`Take the train to Cleveland and the fast ferry over; whales pass the North Gorge from June to November.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`North Stradbroke Island`},{id:`moreton-island-tangalooma`,name:`Moreton Island & Tangalooma Wrecks`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`day-trip`,`island`,`snorkelling`,`sand-dunes`,`wrecks`],area:`Moreton Island (Moreton Bay)`,lat:-27.17667,lng:153.37583,durationHours:9,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:80,rating:4,description:`A day cruise to a sand island with clear water around a line of sunken wrecks for snorkelling, plus sand tobogganing on huge dunes.`,tip:`Book a day cruise with snorkel gear included; ferries leave from Pinkenba near the airport.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Moreton Island`},{id:`australia-zoo`,name:`Australia Zoo`,category:`family`,tags:[`day-trip`,`wildlife`,`crocodiles`,`kids`,`iconic`],area:`Beerwah (Sunshine Coast)`,lat:-26.8366,lng:152.9595,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:48,rating:4,description:`The Irwin family's famous zoo, with daily crocodile shows in the Crocoseum and big walk-through areas of Australian and African animals.`,tip:`Check the show times on arrival and plan around the midday Wildlife Warriors show; the zoo runs a shuttle from Beerwah station.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Australia Zoo`},{id:`glass-house-mountains`,name:`Glass House Mountains`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`views`,`hiking`,`volcanic`],area:`Sunshine Coast hinterland`,lat:-26.93173,lng:152.89475,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A cluster of dramatic volcanic plugs rising from the plains, with short walks and a lookout over the peaks.`,tip:`Easy to combine with Australia Zoo; Mount Ngungun is the best short summit hike for most visitors.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Glass House Mountains`},{id:`noosa-national-park`,name:`Noosa National Park`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`coastal-walk`,`beaches`,`koalas`,`surf`],area:`Noosa Heads (Sunshine Coast)`,lat:-26.38444,lng:153.11278,durationHours:9,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A headland of rainforest and coastal trails above surf beaches and rocky bays, next to the stylish resort town of Noosa Heads.`,tip:`Walk the coastal track to Hell's Gates and watch for koalas in the trees and dolphins below.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Noosa National Park`},{id:`surfers-paradise`,name:`Surfers Paradise (Gold Coast)`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`day-trip`,`beach`,`surf`,`high-rise`],area:`Gold Coast`,lat:-28,lng:153.4166,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The Gold Coast's high-rise heart, fronting a long patrolled surf beach, with Burleigh Heads and its headland park a short tram and bus ride south.`,tip:`Take the train to Helensvale and the G:link tram; swim between the red and yellow flags.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Surfers Paradise`},{id:`tamborine-mountain`,name:`Tamborine Mountain`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`rainforest`,`waterfalls`,`wineries`],area:`Gold Coast hinterland`,lat:-27.92173,lng:153.20055,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:15,rating:3,description:`A rainforest-covered plateau with waterfall walks, a treetop skywalk and the craft shops, cafés and wineries of Gallery Walk.`,tip:`You will need a car or tour; Curtis Falls is a short, easy rainforest walk.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Tamborine Mountain`},{id:`springbrook-natural-bridge`,name:`Natural Bridge, Springbrook National Park`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`rainforest`,`waterfall`,`glow-worms`],area:`Gold Coast hinterland`,lat:-28.2205,lng:153.2286,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A waterfall plunging through the roof of a basalt cave in World Heritage rainforest, lit by glow-worms after dark.`,tip:`Visit after dusk on a tour to see the glow-worms; no torches or flash near them.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Natural Bridge, Queensland`}],foods:[{name:`Moreton Bay bugs`,description:`Flat, sweet-fleshed slipper lobsters from the bay, served grilled with garlic butter or split on a seafood platter.`},{name:`Barramundi`,description:`A firm, mild white fish from northern waters, usually pan-fried with crisp skin or grilled whole.`},{name:`Queensland steak`,description:`Grass- or grain-fed beef from the Darling Downs, chargrilled pub-style with chips, salad and a sauce of your choice.`},{name:`Fish and chips`,description:`Battered or grilled local fish with hot chips, best eaten from the paper on a bayside foreshore.`},{name:`Lamington`,description:`A Queensland-born square of sponge cake dipped in chocolate and rolled in coconut, sometimes with jam or cream inside.`},{name:`Mango`,description:`Queensland mangoes are a summer ritual from November, eaten fresh, in smoothies or in ice cream and desserts.`}]},{id:`cairns`,name:`Cairns`,lat:-16.9203,lng:145.771,timezone:`Australia/Brisbane`,tagline:`Gateway to the Great Barrier Reef and ancient rainforest`,description:`A laid-back tropical city on Trinity Inlet where two World Heritage wonders meet: the Great Barrier Reef offshore and the Wet Tropics rainforest on the ranges behind. Days are spent snorkelling the outer reef, riding up to Kuranda or exploring the Daintree, with evenings by the free Esplanade Lagoon and the night markets.`,idealDays:[3,6],places:[{id:`esplanade-lagoon`,name:`Cairns Esplanade Lagoon`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`free`,`swimming`,`lagoon`,`kids`,`iconic`],area:`Esplanade`,lat:-16.9195,lng:145.78,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A big, free saltwater swimming lagoon on the waterfront, with lifeguards, sandy edges and palm-shaded lawns, the safe way to swim in the city.`,tip:`The sea here is mudflat and home to crocodiles, so swim in the lagoon; it closes for maintenance for a few weeks some winters.`,indoor:!1},{id:`esplanade-boardwalk`,name:`Cairns Esplanade Boardwalk`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`walking`,`birdwatching`,`sunrise`,`waterfront`],area:`Esplanade`,lat:-16.912,lng:145.7769,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A long seafront promenade over the mudflats, alive with pelicans, herons and migratory shorebirds, with BBQs, fitness stations and sea views.`,tip:`Walk it at low tide early morning for the birds, or in the evening when flying foxes cross the sky.`,indoor:!1},{id:`muddys-playground`,name:`Muddy's Playground`,category:`family`,tags:[`free`,`kids`,`playground`,`water-play`],area:`Esplanade`,lat:-16.9148,lng:145.777,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:2,description:`A free waterfront playground with water-play fountains, climbing nets and shady picnic areas on the Esplanade.`,tip:`Bring swimmers for the water-play area; there are BBQs and a café alongside.`,indoor:!1},{id:`cairns-night-markets`,name:`Cairns Night Markets`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`night-market`,`souvenirs`,`food-court`,`massage`,`rainy-day`],area:`City Centre (Esplanade)`,lat:-16.9215,lng:145.779,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`A covered evening arcade off the Esplanade with souvenir stalls, cheap massages and an Asian-style food court.`,tip:`Open every evening; eat in the food court, then stroll the lit-up Esplanade.`,indoor:!0},{id:`cairns-aquarium`,name:`Cairns Aquarium`,category:`family`,tags:[`aquarium`,`reef`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`City Centre`,lat:-16.9266,lng:145.7745,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`A modern aquarium tracing the water from rainforest rivers to the outer reef, with a huge oceanarium and a walk-through tunnel.`,tip:`A good rainy-day or post-flight option; the daily talks and feeding sessions are worth timing your visit around.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Cairns Aquarium`},{id:`cairns-art-gallery`,name:`Cairns Art Gallery`,category:`museum`,tags:[`free`,`art`,`indigenous`,`rainy-day`,`heritage`],area:`City Centre`,lat:-16.9232,lng:145.7779,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A free gallery in a heritage building focusing on the art of Far North Queensland, including strong Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander work.`,tip:`Entry is free; it has short Sunday hours, and Perrotta's café out front is good for lunch.`,indoor:!0},{id:`cairns-museum`,name:`Cairns Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`heritage`,`rainy-day`,`small`],area:`City Centre`,lat:-16.9225,lng:145.7756,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:2,description:`The city's history museum in the old School of Arts building, covering First Nations culture, gold rush days and the cane railways.`,tip:`Head up to the rooftop viewing deck for a look over City Place; closed Sundays.`,indoor:!0},{id:`rustys-markets`,name:`Rusty's Markets`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`tropical-fruit`,`local`,`weekend`,`rainy-day`],area:`City Centre (Grafton Street)`,lat:-16.9227,lng:145.7729,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A big, covered weekend produce market piled with tropical fruit you rarely see elsewhere, plus food stalls, coffee and local honey.`,tip:`Open Friday to Sunday mornings; try rambutans, mangosteen or a fresh tropical fruit smoothie.`,indoor:!0},{id:`esplanade-markets`,name:`Cairns Esplanade Markets`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`free`,`markets`,`crafts`,`saturday`],area:`Esplanade`,lat:-16.9195,lng:145.7788,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:2,description:`A Saturday morning craft and art market under the trees along the Esplanade, selling local jewellery, art and clothing.`,tip:`Saturdays only; combine with a swim at the lagoon next door.`,indoor:!1},{id:`marlin-marina`,name:`Marlin Marina & Waterfront`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`waterfront`,`sunset`,`dining`,`boats`],area:`Marlin Marina`,lat:-16.9225,lng:145.782,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The busy marina where the reef boats berth, lined with a boardwalk of seafood restaurants and bars looking across Trinity Inlet.`,tip:`Come in the late afternoon to watch the reef boats return, then stay for dinner on the boardwalk.`,indoor:!1},{id:`salt-house`,name:`Sunset Drinks at Salt House`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bar`,`sunset`,`waterfront`,`live-music`],area:`Marlin Marina`,lat:-16.9201,lng:145.7825,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:3,description:`A big open-air bar and restaurant on the marina point, with day beds, fire features and views over the inlet to the ranges.`,tip:`Arrive before sunset for a waterfront seat; weekends often have live music or DJs.`,indoor:!1},{id:`cairns-performing-arts-centre`,name:`Cairns Performing Arts Centre (CPAC)`,category:`culture`,tags:[`theatre`,`music`,`shows`,`rainy-day`],area:`City Centre (Sheridan Street)`,lat:-16.9258,lng:145.7716,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:55,rating:2,description:`The city's modern theatre, hosting touring productions, music, dance and comedy, beside the outdoor Munro Martin Parklands stage.`,tip:`Check the programme before you travel; outdoor concerts in Munro Martin Parklands next door are a balmy dry-season treat.`,indoor:!0},{id:`tanks-arts-centre`,name:`Tanks Arts Centre`,category:`culture`,tags:[`arts`,`live-music`,`markets`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Edge Hill`,lat:-16.9017,lng:145.7484,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:3,description:`Three huge Second World War fuel tanks converted into an arts venue for gigs, theatre and exhibitions, tucked into the rainforest by the Botanic Gardens.`,tip:`Check the gig guide; the Tanks Market runs on the last Sunday of the month in the dry season.`,indoor:!0},{id:`cairns-botanic-gardens`,name:`Cairns Botanic Gardens`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`gardens`,`rainforest`,`walking`,`birdwatching`],area:`Edge Hill`,lat:-16.899,lng:145.7505,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Lush tropical gardens of palms, gingers and orchids, with boardwalks through rainforest and mangroves to the Centenary Lakes.`,tip:`Join a free guided walk from the visitor centre, then have breakfast at the gardens café.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Flecker Botanical Gardens`},{id:`mount-whitfield-red-arrow`,name:`Mount Whitfield Red Arrow Walk`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`free`,`hiking`,`views`,`rainforest`],area:`Edge Hill`,lat:-16.8974,lng:145.7489,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A steep rainforest loop above the Botanic Gardens with lookouts over the city, airport and Coral Sea.`,tip:`Start early to beat the heat and bring water; the longer Blue Arrow circuit suits fit hikers.`,indoor:!1},{id:`crystal-cascades`,name:`Crystal Cascades`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`swimming`,`waterfall`,`rainforest`,`local`],area:`Redlynch`,lat:-16.9603,lng:145.6812,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A series of clear rainforest pools and small falls on Freshwater Creek, a favourite local swimming hole 20 minutes from town.`,tip:`Stay out of the water after heavy rain, when currents are dangerous; weekdays are quietest.`,indoor:!1},{id:`palm-cove`,name:`Palm Cove`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`free`,`beach`,`resort`,`cafes`],area:`Northern Beaches`,lat:-16.7445,lng:145.6715,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A pretty, palm-lined beach village of resorts and cafés under giant paperbark trees, half an hour north of the city.`,tip:`Swim inside the stinger nets, especially from November to May; the jetty is a good spot at sunrise.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Palm Cove, Queensland`},{id:`trinity-beach`,name:`Trinity Beach`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`free`,`beach`,`swimming`,`local`],area:`Northern Beaches`,lat:-16.7884,lng:145.698,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A relaxed beach suburb with a sheltered crescent of sand, a stinger net and a strip of casual cafés facing the sea.`,tip:`Less busy than Palm Cove; buses run from the city centre.`,indoor:!1},{id:`great-barrier-reef-cruise`,name:`Outer Great Barrier Reef Cruise`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`day-trip`,`snorkelling`,`diving`,`reef`,`iconic`,`bucket-list`],area:`Outer Reef`,lat:-16.869,lng:146.21,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:180,rating:5,description:`A full-day boat trip to the outer reef to snorkel or dive among coral gardens, giant clams, turtles and clouds of tropical fish.`,tip:`Boats leave from the Reef Fleet Terminal around 8am; wear a stinger suit from November to May and take seasickness tablets if prone.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Great Barrier Reef`},{id:`green-island`,name:`Green Island`,category:`nature`,tags:[`island`,`snorkelling`,`beach`,`glass-bottom-boat`,`kids`],area:`Green Island (Reef)`,lat:-16.7581,lng:145.972,durationHours:4.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:75,rating:4,description:`A small coral cay just 45 minutes by boat, ringed with white sand and reef you can snorkel straight from the beach.`,tip:`A good choice for families and non-swimmers, with glass-bottom boats; go early before the day-trip crowds.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Green Island (Queensland)`},{id:`fitzroy-island`,name:`Fitzroy Island`,category:`nature`,tags:[`island`,`snorkelling`,`hiking`,`turtles`],area:`Fitzroy Island (Reef)`,lat:-16.9312,lng:145.992,durationHours:4.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:60,rating:4,description:`A rainforest-covered continental island with coral beaches, a turtle rehabilitation centre and a walk up to a lighthouse lookout.`,tip:`Snorkel off Nudey Beach and visit the turtle hospital tour if it is running.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Fitzroy Island (Queensland)`},{id:`kuranda-skyrail-railway`,name:`Kuranda Scenic Railway & Skyrail`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`day-trip`,`train`,`cable-car`,`rainforest`,`iconic`,`views`],area:`Kuranda`,lat:-16.819,lng:145.6369,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:110,rating:5,description:`Ride a heritage train up past waterfalls and the Barron Gorge to the mountain village of Kuranda, then glide back over the rainforest canopy by cable car.`,tip:`Take the train up in the morning and Skyrail down; in Kuranda, see the markets and the Barron Falls lookout.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Kuranda Scenic Railway`},{id:`rainforestation`,name:`Rainforestation Nature Park`,category:`family`,tags:[`wildlife`,`koalas`,`army-duck`,`kids`,`culture`],area:`Kuranda`,lat:-16.8186,lng:145.6517,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:3,description:`A rainforest park outside Kuranda with amphibious Army Duck rides, a wildlife area with koalas, and an Aboriginal culture show.`,tip:`Easily combined with a Kuranda day; shuttles run from the village.`,indoor:!1},{id:`barron-falls`,name:`Barron Falls Lookout`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`waterfall`,`rainforest`,`views`,`boardwalk`],area:`Kuranda`,lat:-16.8426,lng:145.6431,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A rainforest boardwalk to lookouts over the Barron Gorge, where the river plunges in a thundering curtain during the wet season.`,tip:`The falls are at their mightiest from January to April; in the dry season the flow can shrink to a trickle.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Barron Falls`},{id:`daintree-cape-tribulation`,name:`Daintree Rainforest & Cape Tribulation`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`rainforest`,`crocodiles`,`beach`,`iconic`],area:`Daintree`,lat:-16.086,lng:145.462,durationHours:10,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:150,rating:5,description:`The world's oldest tropical rainforest meeting the reef at Cape Tribulation, reached via a croc-spotting river cruise and the Daintree River ferry.`,tip:`A guided day tour is easiest and usually includes Mossman Gorge; never swim in creeks or at the beaches here because of crocodiles.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Daintree Rainforest`},{id:`hartleys-crocodile-adventures`,name:`Hartley's Crocodile Adventures`,category:`family`,tags:[`crocodiles`,`wildlife`,`kids`,`boat-cruise`],area:`Wangetti`,lat:-16.6461,lng:145.5578,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`A wildlife park in lagoon and wetland country, best known for its crocodile attack shows and boat cruise through a croc-filled lagoon.`,tip:`Plan your day around the crocodile feeding and lagoon cruise times; it sits on the coast road to Port Douglas.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hartley's Crocodile Adventures`},{id:`skypark-bungy`,name:`Skypark by AJ Hackett`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`bungy`,`thrill`,`rainforest`,`bucket-list`],area:`Smithfield`,lat:-16.816,lng:145.6878,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:125,rating:3,description:`Australia's only bungy tower, a 50-metre jump over the rainforest, plus a giant jungle swing for less brave adventurers.`,tip:`Free transfers usually run from Cairns and Palm Cove; minimum age 10.`,indoor:!1},{id:`hot-air-balloon-mareeba`,name:`Hot Air Ballooning over the Tablelands`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`balloon`,`sunrise`,`views`,`bucket-list`],area:`Mareeba`,lat:-16.99,lng:145.423,durationHours:4.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:230,rating:3,description:`A sunrise balloon flight over the farms and outback edge of the Atherton Tablelands, often with kangaroos bounding below.`,tip:`Pick-ups from Cairns are around 4am; flights depend on the weather, so book early in your stay.`,indoor:!1},{id:`babinda-boulders`,name:`Babinda Boulders`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`rainforest`,`swimming-hole`,`walking`],area:`Babinda`,lat:-17.345,lng:145.872,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Clear water rushing between smooth granite boulders in rainforest an hour south of Cairns, with a calm swimming area at the top.`,tip:`Swim only in the marked swimming area; the boulders downstream are slippery and dangerous.`,indoor:!1},{id:`josephine-falls`,name:`Josephine Falls`,category:`nature`,tags:[`free`,`waterfall`,`rainforest`,`swimming-hole`],area:`Wooroonooran National Park`,lat:-17.4336,lng:145.8586,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A beautiful series of cascades tumbling off Queensland's highest mountain, reached by a short rainforest walk.`,tip:`Pair it with Babinda Boulders; obey closures after rain, as flash floods are sudden here.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Josephine Falls`},{id:`ellis-beach-coast-drive`,name:`Captain Cook Highway Coast Drive & Ellis Beach`,category:`nature`,tags:[`scenic-drive`,`beach`,`views`,`photo`],area:`Ellis Beach`,lat:-16.725,lng:145.659,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The winding coastal road north of Cairns, squeezed between rainforest and sea, with lookouts and the palm-fringed sweep of Ellis Beach.`,tip:`Stop at Rex Lookout for the view; continue to Port Douglas if you have the whole day.`,indoor:!1},{id:`reef-scenic-flight`,name:`Great Barrier Reef Scenic Flight`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`helicopter`,`views`,`reef`,`bucket-list`],area:`Cairns Airport`,lat:-16.875,lng:145.754,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:200,rating:3,description:`A helicopter or light-plane flight over coral reefs, sand cays and the coastline, showing the scale of the reef from above.`,tip:`Midday light shows the reef colours best; several operators fly from the airport and the marina.`,indoor:!1}],foods:[{name:`Barramundi`,description:`A firm, mild white fish from tropical waters, best pan-fried with crisp skin or as grilled fish and chips.`},{name:`Mud crab`,description:`Big, sweet-fleshed crabs from the mangroves, served whole with chilli, garlic or black pepper.`},{name:`Fresh prawns`,description:`Local tiger and banana prawns bought cooked by the kilo and peeled on the waterfront with a cold drink.`},{name:`Coral trout`,description:`A prized red reef fish with delicate white flesh, steamed Asian-style or pan-fried in Cairns seafood restaurants.`},{name:`Tropical fruit`,description:`Mangoes, rambutans, mangosteen, dragon fruit and black sapote from the Tablelands and coast, at their best at Rusty's Markets.`},{name:`Kangaroo and native bush foods`,description:`Lean kangaroo steak and dishes using native ingredients like lemon myrtle, finger lime and wattleseed.`}]},{id:`perth`,name:`Perth`,lat:-31.9523,lng:115.8613,timezone:`Australia/Perth`,tagline:`Sunny river city of white beaches, Kings Park and Fremantle`,description:`The world's most isolated big city, set on the broad Swan River with Indian Ocean beaches on its doorstep. Mornings in vast Kings Park, swims at Cottesloe and sunsets over the sea fit easily around a compact CBD; port town Fremantle adds convict history, markets and seafood, and Rottnest's quokkas are a short ferry ride away.`,idealDays:[3,6],places:[{id:`kings-park`,name:`Kings Park and Botanic Garden`,category:`nature`,tags:[`iconic`,`park`,`viewpoint`,`botanic-garden`,`wildflowers`,`free`,`sunset`],area:`Kings Park`,lat:-31.96084,lng:115.84466,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`One of the world's largest inner-city parks, mostly native bushland, with lookouts over the Swan River and skyline, a superb garden of Western Australian plants and a glass-and-steel treetop walkway.`,tip:`Start at the State War Memorial lookout on Fraser Avenue, then walk the Federation Walkway. Spring (September to November) brings the wildflowers; free guided walks leave daily.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Kings Park, Western Australia`},{id:`elizabeth-quay`,name:`Elizabeth Quay`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`waterfront`,`free`,`night-view`,`river`,`photo-spot`],area:`CBD`,lat:-31.9578,lng:115.85693,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A riverside inlet carved into the city's edge, ringed by a footbridge, restaurants and public art, with ferries across the river to South Perth.`,tip:`Take the cheap Transperth ferry to Mends Street and back for the best skyline view, especially at dusk.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Elizabeth Quay`},{id:`bell-tower`,name:`The Bell Tower`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`bells`,`viewpoint`,`rainy-day`,`river`],area:`CBD`,lat:-31.95896,lng:115.85823,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:3,description:`A glass spire on the riverfront housing the Swan Bells, twelve of them from London's St Martin-in-the-Fields, with an observation deck over Elizabeth Quay.`,tip:`Time your visit for a ringing session (usually around midday on some days) and try handling a bell yourself.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Swan Bells`},{id:`perth-mint`,name:`The Perth Mint`,category:`museum`,tags:[`gold`,`history`,`heritage`,`rainy-day`],area:`East Perth`,lat:-31.95685,lng:115.86941,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:3,description:`Australia's oldest operating mint, in an 1899 limestone building, where you can watch a live gold pour and see a huge collection of nuggets and coins.`,tip:`Book the gold-pour session online; it runs at set times through the day.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Perth Mint`},{id:`art-gallery-of-western-australia`,name:`Art Gallery of Western Australia`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`aboriginal-art`,`free`,`rainy-day`,`rooftop`],area:`Perth Cultural Centre`,lat:-31.9507,lng:115.8611,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The state gallery, strong on Aboriginal art and Western Australian painting, crowned by a rooftop bar and sculpture terrace looking over the city.`,tip:`General entry is free; closed on Tuesdays. Head up to the rooftop for a drink afterwards.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Art Gallery of Western Australia`},{id:`wa-museum-boola-bardip`,name:`WA Museum Boola Bardip`,category:`museum`,tags:[`museum`,`natural-history`,`aboriginal-culture`,`kids`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Perth Cultural Centre`,lat:-31.94951,lng:115.8618,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A striking modern museum wrapped around heritage buildings, telling Western Australia's story from Aboriginal culture to ocean life, under a full blue-whale skeleton.`,tip:`Entry to the permanent galleries is free; special exhibitions are ticketed.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Western Australian Museum`},{id:`pica`,name:`Perth Institute of Contemporary Arts`,category:`culture`,tags:[`art`,`contemporary`,`free`,`rainy-day`,`bar`],area:`Perth Cultural Centre`,lat:-31.94983,lng:115.86026,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:2,description:`An experimental arts space in a red-brick former boys' school, with free exhibitions, performance and a popular bar on the front lawn.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Perth Institute of Contemporary Arts`},{id:`yagan-square`,name:`Yagan Square`,category:`food`,tags:[`food-hall`,`public-space`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`CBD`,lat:-31.95059,lng:115.85856,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:2,description:`A modern public square linking the CBD and Northbridge, with a covered food hall, a giant digital tower and a sculpture honouring the Noongar warrior Yagan.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Yagan Square`},{id:`london-court`,name:`London Court`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`arcade`,`heritage`,`photo-spot`,`free`,`quirky`],area:`CBD`,lat:-31.9543,lng:115.85918,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:2,description:`A 1937 mock-Tudor shopping lane between Hay Street and St Georges Terrace, complete with half-timbered gables and mechanical clocks.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`London Court`},{id:`hay-murray-street-malls`,name:`Hay Street and Murray Street Malls`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`shopping`,`pedestrian`,`arcades`,`free`],area:`CBD`,lat:-31.9533,lng:115.858,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:2,description:`Two parallel pedestrian malls at the heart of the CBD, linked by arcades and lined with department stores, Australian fashion labels and street performers.`,indoor:!1},{id:`st-marys-cathedral`,name:`St Mary's Cathedral`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`architecture`,`heritage`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`CBD`,lat:-31.95542,lng:115.86659,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:2,description:`Perth's Catholic cathedral, a Gothic Revival nave joined to a light-filled modern extension, set on a green rise at the east end of the city.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`St Mary's Cathedral, Perth`},{id:`northbridge`,name:`Northbridge`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`clubs`,`restaurants`,`live-music`,`late-night`],area:`Northbridge`,lat:-31.948,lng:115.85729,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`Perth's after-dark heart just north of the railway, packed with small bars, live-music venues, clubs and cheap Asian eateries around William and James streets.`,tip:`Friday and Saturday nights are liveliest; carry ID, as door checks are strict.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Northbridge, Western Australia`},{id:`crown-perth`,name:`Crown Perth`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`resort`,`bars`,`restaurants`,`shows`,`night-view`],area:`Burswood`,lat:-31.96027,lng:115.8944,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:2,description:`A riverside entertainment resort across the Swan from the city, with a theatre for big shows, late bars, rooftop views and some of Perth’s best-known restaurants beside Optus Stadium.`,tip:`Book a show or dinner ahead; smart-casual dress is expected at the bars, and the casino floor itself is 18+ only.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Crown Perth`},{id:`his-majestys-theatre`,name:`His Majesty's Theatre`,category:`culture`,tags:[`theatre`,`opera`,`ballet`,`heritage`,`rainy-day`],area:`CBD`,lat:-31.95305,lng:115.85438,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:60,rating:3,description:`An ornate Edwardian theatre from 1904, home of WA Opera and the West Australian Ballet and the city's main stage for touring musicals.`,tip:`Check the programme and book ahead; the small theatre museum is free on weekdays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`His Majesty's Theatre, Perth`},{id:`perth-zoo`,name:`Perth Zoo`,category:`family`,tags:[`zoo`,`kids`,`australian-animals`,`river`],area:`South Perth`,lat:-31.977,lng:115.85463,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:3,description:`A leafy zoo across the river from the city, with an Australian bushwalk of kangaroos and wallabies, plus orangutans, African savannah and Asian rainforest zones.`,tip:`Arrive by ferry from Elizabeth Quay to Mends Street, a short walk away; mornings are cooler and the animals busier.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Perth Zoo`},{id:`heirisson-island`,name:`Heirisson Island`,category:`nature`,tags:[`kangaroos`,`wildlife`,`free`,`river`,`hidden-gem`],area:`East Perth`,lat:-31.96532,lng:115.8833,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A grassy island in the Swan River, reached by the Causeway, where a small mob of western grey kangaroos lives in a fenced sanctuary close to the city.`,tip:`Come early morning or near dusk when the kangaroos are grazing; do not feed them.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Heirisson Island`},{id:`cottesloe-beach`,name:`Cottesloe Beach`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`beach`,`sunset`,`swimming`,`iconic`,`free`],area:`Cottesloe`,lat:-31.9954,lng:115.7512,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Perth's favourite beach: calm turquoise water, a grassy Norfolk pine-lined terrace and the landmark Indiana Teahouse, with the sun setting straight into the Indian Ocean.`,tip:`Swim between the flags; the afternoon sea breeze arrives around midday, so morning swims are calmest. Stay for sunset with fish and chips.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Cottesloe Beach`},{id:`scarborough-beach`,name:`Scarborough Beach`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`beach`,`surf`,`sunset`,`free`,`foreshore`],area:`Scarborough`,lat:-31.89705,lng:115.75506,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A lively surf beach with a revamped foreshore of pools, skate park, bars and cafés, busier and younger than Cottesloe.`,tip:`Waves can be strong; swim between the flags. The Sunset Hill lookout is a good spot as the sun goes down.`,indoor:!1},{id:`hillarys-boat-harbour`,name:`Hillarys Boat Harbour`,category:`family`,tags:[`marina`,`beach`,`kids`,`restaurants`,`free`],area:`Hillarys`,lat:-31.82406,lng:115.73612,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A family-friendly marina in the northern suburbs with a sheltered swimming beach, boardwalk shops, fish and chips and sunset views.`,tip:`Pair it with AQWA next door; the protected beach inside the harbour is ideal for small children.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hillarys Boat Harbour`},{id:`aqwa`,name:`AQWA - The Aquarium of Western Australia`,category:`family`,tags:[`aquarium`,`sharks`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`Hillarys`,lat:-31.82678,lng:115.73786,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:3,description:`Australia's largest aquarium follows the WA coastline from the tropical north to the cold south, with a walk-through shark tunnel and coral reef.`,tip:`Tickets are cheaper online; join a scheduled feeding talk.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Aquarium of Western Australia`},{id:`caversham-wildlife-park`,name:`Caversham Wildlife Park`,category:`family`,tags:[`wildlife`,`kangaroos`,`koalas`,`wombats`,`kids`],area:`Whiteman Park`,lat:-31.8339,lng:115.94991,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`A large wildlife park in Whiteman Park where you can hand-feed kangaroos, meet wombats and see koalas up close, plus a farm show with sheep shearing.`,tip:`Arrive at opening and check the schedule for koala and wombat encounters; it is a 30-minute drive from the city.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Caversham Wildlife Park`},{id:`yanchep-national-park`,name:`Yanchep National Park`,category:`nature`,tags:[`koalas`,`caves`,`kangaroos`,`bushwalk`,`aboriginal-culture`],area:`Yanchep`,lat:-31.54589,lng:115.68036,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`Bushland and wetlands 50 km north of the city with a koala boardwalk, wild kangaroos on the lawns, limestone caves and Aboriginal cultural experiences.`,tip:`Entry is charged per vehicle. Crystal Cave tours run at set times; book on arrival.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Yanchep National Park`},{id:`fremantle-prison`,name:`Fremantle Prison`,category:`museum`,tags:[`unesco`,`convict-history`,`heritage`,`tour`,`iconic`],area:`Fremantle`,lat:-32.05508,lng:115.75271,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`A UNESCO-listed convict-built prison that held inmates from the 1850s until 1991, explored on guided tours of the cell blocks, gallows and flooded tunnels beneath.`,tip:`The standard day tour is enough for most; the tunnels tour (book ahead) adds a boat ride underground, and torchlight tours run some evenings.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Fremantle Prison`},{id:`fremantle-markets`,name:`Fremantle Markets`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`market`,`heritage`,`street-food`,`souvenirs`,`iconic`,`free`],area:`Fremantle`,lat:-32.05597,lng:115.74958,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A Victorian market hall from 1897 packed with craft stalls, buskers, fresh produce and food vendors, a Fremantle institution.`,tip:`Open Friday to Sunday (and some public holidays) only; go hungry and browse the produce hall at the back.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Fremantle Markets`},{id:`wa-maritime-museum`,name:`WA Maritime Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`maritime`,`museum`,`submarine`,`america-s-cup`,`rainy-day`],area:`Fremantle`,lat:-32.05473,lng:115.73921,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`A sail-shaped museum on Victoria Quay telling WA's ocean story, home to the America's Cup-winning yacht Australia II; the Oberon-class submarine Ovens can be toured next door.`,tip:`Submarine tours are separately ticketed and run at set times; buy a combined ticket.`,indoor:!0},{id:`round-house-fremantle`,name:`The Round House`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`heritage`,`convict-history`,`viewpoint`,`free`],area:`Fremantle`,lat:-32.05612,lng:115.74127,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`WA's oldest surviving public building, a twelve-sided 1831 jail on a headland at the end of High Street, with the time ball fired at 1pm each day.`,tip:`Be there just before 1pm for the time-ball drop and cannon firing; entry is by gold-coin donation.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Round House (Western Australia)`},{id:`bathers-beach`,name:`Bathers Beach`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`beach`,`sunset`,`free`,`art-galleries`,`bars`],area:`Fremantle`,lat:-32.05696,lng:115.74109,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A small sheltered beach below the Round House, backed by artists' studios and a beach bar, the closest swim to Fremantle's centre.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Bathers Beach, Fremantle`},{id:`fremantle-cappuccino-strip`,name:`Cappuccino Strip, South Terrace`,category:`food`,tags:[`cafes`,`people-watching`,`heritage`,`free`],area:`Fremantle`,lat:-32.0556,lng:115.74712,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:3,description:`Fremantle's café row along South Terrace, where old Italian espresso bars and pavement tables fill with locals from breakfast until late.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`South Terrace, Fremantle`},{id:`fremantle-fishing-boat-harbour`,name:`Fremantle Fishing Boat Harbour`,category:`food`,tags:[`seafood`,`fish-and-chips`,`waterfront`,`sunset`],area:`Fremantle`,lat:-32.062,lng:115.74522,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`A working harbour whose boardwalk is lined with fish-and-chip shops, seafood restaurants and the Little Creatures brewery, at its best around sunset.`,tip:`Keep an eye on the seagulls when you carry your chips outside.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Fremantle Fishing Boat Harbour`},{id:`fremantle-arts-centre`,name:`Fremantle Arts Centre`,category:`culture`,tags:[`art`,`heritage`,`gardens`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Fremantle`,lat:-32.04768,lng:115.75398,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Free contemporary art exhibitions in a Gothic limestone former asylum built by convicts, with a shady garden café and craft shop.`,tip:`Check for summer Sunday music sessions on the lawns.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Fremantle Arts Centre`},{id:`rottnest-island`,name:`Rottnest Island Day Trip`,localName:`Wadjemup`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`quokkas`,`cycling`,`snorkelling`,`beach`,`iconic`],area:`Rottnest Island`,lat:-31.99564,lng:115.54353,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:75,rating:5,description:`A car-free island a short ferry ride offshore, ringed by turquoise bays; cycle between snorkelling coves and meet the famously smiley quokkas.`,tip:`Book ferry and bike hire together and catch the first boat. Do not touch or feed the quokkas, which is illegal; bring water and sun cover as shade is scarce.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Rottnest Island`},{id:`pinnacles`,name:`The Pinnacles Desert Day Trip`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`desert`,`limestone`,`photo-spot`,`sunset`,`iconic`],area:`Nambung National Park`,lat:-30.60306,lng:115.15562,durationHours:10,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`Thousands of eerie limestone spires rising from yellow sand in Nambung National Park, about a two-and-a-half-hour drive north along the coast.`,tip:`Entry is per vehicle; the loop drive and walks take about an hour. Stop for lobster in Cervantes and at the Lancelin sand dunes on the way.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`The Pinnacles (Western Australia)`},{id:`swan-valley`,name:`Swan Valley Wineries`,category:`food`,tags:[`day-trip`,`wine`,`brewery`,`chocolate`,`food-trail`],area:`Swan Valley`,lat:-31.8687,lng:115.99276,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:4,description:`WA's oldest wine region, 30 minutes from the city, with a loop of cellar doors, breweries, chocolate and nougat makers and farm-gate cafés.`,tip:`Do not drive between tastings: join a tour or take the ferry-and-coach trips that run up the river from the city.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Swan Valley (Western Australia)`}],foods:[{name:`Western Rock Lobster`,description:`WA's prized crayfish, caught along the coast north of Perth and served grilled, in rolls or chilled with garlic butter.`},{name:`Fish and Chips`,description:`Battered or grilled local fish such as snapper, dhufish or barramundi with hot chips, best eaten by the water in Fremantle or Cottesloe.`},{name:`Chilli Mussels`,description:`A Fremantle classic: local blue mussels steamed in a spicy tomato and chilli sauce, served with crusty bread to mop it up.`},{name:`Meat Pie`,description:`The Australian hand pie of minced beef in rich gravy under flaky pastry, topped with tomato sauce.`},{name:`Flat White`,description:`Espresso with velvety steamed milk, the everyday order in Perth's serious café culture.`},{name:`Pavlova`,description:`A crisp-shelled, marshmallow-soft meringue topped with whipped cream and fresh fruit, a staple of Australian celebrations.`}]},{id:`adelaide`,name:`Adelaide`,lat:-34.9285,lng:138.6007,timezone:`Australia/Adelaide`,tagline:`Leafy festival city ringed by parklands, beaches and wine country`,description:`A relaxed, grid-planned capital wrapped in green parklands, with grand galleries and museums lined up along North Terrace, one of the world's great covered food markets and a tram straight to the beach at Glenelg. Its real trump card is what lies within an hour's drive: the Adelaide Hills, the Barossa Valley and McLaren Vale, some of Australia's finest wine regions.`,idealDays:[3,6],places:[{id:`adelaide-central-market`,name:`Adelaide Central Market`,category:`food`,tags:[`iconic`,`market`,`foodie`,`rainy-day`,`local-produce`],area:`Central Market`,lat:-34.92985,lng:138.59649,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:5,description:`One of the largest undercover fresh-produce markets in the Southern Hemisphere, trading since 1869: some 70 stalls of cheese, smallgoods, bakeries, coffee and South Australian fruit under one roof.`,tip:`Closed Sundays and Mondays. Come hungry on a Friday or Saturday morning, when it is at its liveliest, and graze your way round.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Adelaide Central Market`},{id:`art-gallery-of-south-australia`,name:`Art Gallery of South Australia`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`aboriginal-art`,`free`,`rainy-day`,`iconic`],area:`North Terrace`,lat:-34.92064,lng:138.60372,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A grand colonial gallery holding one of Australia's finest collections, from Tom Roberts and Hans Heysen landscapes to outstanding Aboriginal art and European old masters.`,tip:`General entry is free and it opens daily from 10am; combine it with the museum next door.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Art Gallery of South Australia`},{id:`south-australian-museum`,name:`South Australian Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`natural-history`,`aboriginal-culture`,`kids`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`North Terrace`,lat:-34.92105,lng:138.60283,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A free natural-history museum famous for its huge Australian Aboriginal Cultures Gallery, plus opalised fossils, a giant squid and the polar explorer Douglas Mawson's Antarctic gear.`,tip:`Start upstairs in the Aboriginal Cultures Gallery, the largest collection of its kind in the world.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`South Australian Museum`},{id:`adelaide-migration-museum`,name:`Migration Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`free`,`rainy-day`,`hidden-gem`],area:`North Terrace`,lat:-34.92004,lng:138.60098,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Housed in the old Destitute Asylum behind North Terrace, this free museum tells the stories of the people who have made South Australia home, from Kaurna country to postwar migrants.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Migration Museum, Adelaide`},{id:`state-library-of-south-australia`,name:`State Library of South Australia (Mortlock Wing)`,category:`culture`,tags:[`library`,`architecture`,`free`,`rainy-day`,`photo-spot`,`hidden-gem`],area:`North Terrace`,lat:-34.92087,lng:138.60193,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The library's 1884 Mortlock Chamber is a gorgeous two-storey reading room of wrought-iron balconies and leather-bound books under a glass lantern roof.`,tip:`Free to wander; go on a weekday morning for a quiet, people-free photo.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`State Library of South Australia`},{id:`adelaide-botanic-garden`,name:`Adelaide Botanic Garden`,category:`nature`,tags:[`garden`,`free`,`park`,`architecture`,`iconic`],area:`Botanic Park`,lat:-34.9179,lng:138.6108,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Fifty hectares of lawns, lily ponds and avenues on the edge of the CBD, with the restored 1877 Palm House, a giant Amazon waterlily pavilion and a Museum of Economic Botany.`,tip:`Free entry; walk through from the East End and on to the National Wine Centre next door.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Adelaide Botanic Garden`},{id:`national-wine-centre`,name:`National Wine Centre of Australia`,category:`food`,tags:[`wine`,`tasting`,`rainy-day`],area:`Botanic Park`,lat:-34.91765,lng:138.616,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`A striking timber-and-glass building at the end of the Botanic Garden with a free exhibition on Australian winemaking and a tasting room pouring wines from every region.`,tip:`Buy a tasting card and pour your own from the self-serve wine stations, a good primer before heading out to the Barossa.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National Wine Centre of Australia`},{id:`adelaide-zoo`,name:`Adelaide Zoo`,category:`family`,tags:[`zoo`,`kids`,`pandas`,`animals`],area:`Botanic Park`,lat:-34.91436,lng:138.60635,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:33,rating:4,description:`Australia's second-oldest zoo, a compact, leafy site by the River Torrens and home to Yi Lan and Xing Qiu, the only giant pandas in the Southern Hemisphere.`,tip:`See the pandas early, when they are most active; book online for a cheaper ticket.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Adelaide Zoo`},{id:`adelaide-oval-roofclimb`,name:`Adelaide Oval and RoofClimb`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`stadium`,`cricket`,`football`,`viewpoint`,`iconic`],area:`Riverbank`,lat:-34.91558,lng:138.59613,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:110,rating:4,description:`One of the world's most beautiful cricket grounds, its heritage scoreboard set beside sweeping modern stands; harness up for RoofClimb across the stadium roof for views to the hills and sea.`,tip:`Twilight climbs are the most dramatic. On a budget, take the cheaper stadium tour or catch a cricket or AFL match.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Adelaide Oval`},{id:`elder-park-riverbank`,name:`Elder Park and the Torrens Riverbank`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`river`,`park`,`free`,`walk`,`kids`],area:`Riverbank`,lat:-34.9187,lng:138.5972,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Riverside lawns with a lacy 1882 rotunda, black swans and paddle boats on the River Torrens, linked by a footbridge to Adelaide Oval.`,tip:`Hire a paddle boat or walk the riverside path at dusk as the Oval and Festival Centre light up.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Elder Park`},{id:`adelaide-festival-centre`,name:`Adelaide Festival Centre`,category:`culture`,tags:[`theatre`,`performing-arts`,`night`,`rainy-day`],area:`Riverbank`,lat:-34.91827,lng:138.5991,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:60,rating:3,description:`Australia's first multi-arts centre, its white geometric roofs on the riverbank hosting theatre, musicals, opera, comedy and the big Adelaide Festival and Fringe in February and March.`,tip:`Check the programme before you go; the free public art in the surrounding plaza is worth a look on the way in.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Adelaide Festival Centre`},{id:`st-peters-cathedral-adelaide`,name:`St Peter's Cathedral`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`architecture`,`free`,`gothic-revival`],area:`North Adelaide`,lat:-34.9133,lng:138.598,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A Gothic Revival Anglican cathedral whose twin spires frame the classic view across Adelaide Oval, with fine stained glass and a heavy peal of bells inside.`,tip:`Free to enter; the postcard shot of spires and Oval is from the Montefiore Hill lookout nearby.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`St Peter's Cathedral, Adelaide`},{id:`rundle-mall`,name:`Rundle Mall`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`shopping`,`free`,`public-art`,`street`],area:`Rundle Mall`,lat:-34.92288,lng:138.60263,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Adelaide's pedestrian shopping street, home to department stores, the bronze pigs of "A Day Out" and the stainless-steel Mall's Balls sculpture.`,tip:`Duck into the arcades off the mall, and stop at the original Haigh's chocolate shop on Beehive Corner.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Rundle Mall`},{id:`adelaide-arcade`,name:`Adelaide Arcade`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`heritage`,`arcade`,`rainy-day`,`architecture`],area:`Rundle Mall`,lat:-34.92285,lng:138.6014,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`An ornate 1885 shopping arcade of mosaic floors, timber shopfronts and a skylit dome, among the first buildings in Adelaide wired for electric light.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Adelaide Arcade`},{id:`rundle-street-east-end`,name:`Rundle Street and the East End`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`dining`,`bars`,`cafes`,`night`,`street`],area:`East End`,lat:-34.92256,lng:138.6076,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:3,description:`The city's café and dining strip, lined with pavement tables, old pubs, gelato and boutiques, and the hub of the Fringe each autumn.`,tip:`Head here for an evening meal and a drink, then wander the laneways off Ebenezer Place.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Rundle Street, Adelaide`},{id:`peel-street-laneway-bars`,name:`Peel Street and Leigh Street laneway bars`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`laneways`,`night`,`cocktails`,`hidden-gem`],area:`West End`,lat:-34.9231,lng:138.5966,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:3,description:`Two narrow West End lanes packed with small bars, wine rooms and buzzy restaurants, the heart of the city's after-dark scene since licensing laws were loosened.`,tip:`Things get going after 6pm from Thursday to Saturday; bar-hop on foot between the two lanes.`,indoor:!1},{id:`gouger-street-dining`,name:`Gouger Street and Chinatown`,category:`food`,tags:[`dining`,`chinatown`,`seafood`,`night`],area:`Central Market`,lat:-34.92965,lng:138.5938,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:3,description:`Adelaide's busiest eat street, running past the Central Market and Chinatown's Moonta Street gate, lined with seafood houses, Asian restaurants and late-opening dumpling bars.`,tip:`Good for an easy dinner without a booking; the Chinatown food court is cheapest.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Gouger Street, Adelaide`},{id:`adelaide-gaol`,name:`Adelaide Gaol`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`prison`,`heritage`,`ghost-tour`],area:`Park Lands West`,lat:-34.9201,lng:138.5829,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:3,description:`A forbidding stone prison that held inmates from 1841 to 1988, with cell blocks, the hanging tower and the graves of executed prisoners on a self-guided trail.`,tip:`Hospital construction next door means access is via Bonython Park off Port Road. Night ghost tours run on set dates; book ahead.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Adelaide Gaol`},{id:`haighs-chocolates-visitor-centre`,name:`Haigh's Chocolates Visitor Centre`,category:`food`,tags:[`chocolate`,`factory-tour`,`free`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`Parkside`,lat:-34.9449,lng:138.6134,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The flagship of Australia's oldest family-owned chocolatier, founded in Adelaide in 1915, where viewing windows look onto the chocolate-makers at work.`,tip:`Free guided tours with tastings run most days but are capped; book online ahead.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Haigh's Chocolates`},{id:`adelaide-farmers-market`,name:`Adelaide Farmers' Market`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`local-produce`,`weekend`,`breakfast`],area:`Wayville`,lat:-34.9464,lng:138.5856,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`A Sunday-morning growers' market at the Adelaide Showground where farmers, bakers and winemakers sell direct, with breakfast stalls and live music.`,tip:`Sundays only, roughly 9am to 1pm, in the Showground's Goyder Pavilion; arrive early for the best produce.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Adelaide Showground`},{id:`glenelg`,name:`Glenelg Beach and Jetty Road`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`beach`,`tram`,`sunset`,`free`,`kids`,`iconic`],area:`Glenelg`,lat:-34.9805,lng:138.5132,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Adelaide's favourite seaside suburb, reached by the vintage-style tram from the city, with a long sandy beach, a jetty and the bustling shops and cafés of Jetty Road.`,tip:`The tram from the city takes about 30 minutes. Stay for sunset over the sea, then fish and chips on the lawns of Moseley Square.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Glenelg, South Australia`},{id:`henley-beach`,name:`Henley Beach`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`beach`,`sunset`,`free`,`jetty`],area:`Henley Beach`,lat:-34.9202,lng:138.4933,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A laid-back alternative to Glenelg, where Henley Square's restaurants and gelato bars open onto a wide beach and jetty facing west over the gulf.`,tip:`Arrive an hour before sunset and walk the jetty; dinner in Henley Square afterwards.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Henley Beach, South Australia`},{id:`adelaide-dolphin-sanctuary-cruise`,name:`Port Adelaide dolphin cruise`,category:`nature`,tags:[`dolphins`,`boat`,`wildlife`,`kids`],area:`Port Adelaide`,lat:-34.844,lng:138.507,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`Short cruises leave Port Adelaide's historic wharf into the Port River, part of the Adelaide Dolphin Sanctuary, where a resident pod of bottlenose dolphins lives right beside the city.`,tip:`Sightings are very likely but not guaranteed; pair the cruise with the Maritime and Railway museums nearby.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Adelaide Dolphin Sanctuary`},{id:`south-australian-maritime-museum`,name:`South Australian Maritime Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`ships`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`lighthouse`],area:`Port Adelaide`,lat:-34.8453,lng:138.5058,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:3,description:`Australia's oldest maritime museum, in an 1850s bond store, with a walk-through ketch, migrant-ship bunks and a climbable red-and-white lighthouse.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`South Australian Maritime Museum`},{id:`national-railway-museum-port-adelaide`,name:`National Railway Museum`,category:`family`,tags:[`trains`,`kids`,`history`,`rainy-day`],area:`Port Adelaide`,lat:-34.8467,lng:138.5017,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:3,description:`Australia's largest railway museum, with more than a hundred steam and diesel locomotives and carriages in big sheds, plus mini-train rides around the yard.`,tip:`Kids love the train rides on weekends and school holidays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National Railway Museum, Port Adelaide`},{id:`carrick-hill`,name:`Carrick Hill`,category:`culture`,tags:[`historic-house`,`garden`,`art`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Springfield`,lat:-34.9797,lng:138.6333,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:17,rating:3,description:`A 1930s manor house built with timber from an English Tudor mansion, filled with British and Australian art and set in formal gardens and bushland at the foot of the hills.`,tip:`Open Wednesday to Sunday, 10am to 4:30pm; the gardens and grounds are lovely in spring.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Carrick Hill`},{id:`waterfall-gully-to-mount-lofty-hike`,name:`Waterfall Gully to Mount Lofty Summit hike`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`hiking`,`waterfall`,`free`,`workout`,`bush`],area:`Adelaide Hills`,lat:-34.9672,lng:138.6771,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Adelaide's favourite hike climbs steeply from First Falls at Waterfall Gully through eucalypt forest to the summit, about 4 km and 400 m up, with koalas sometimes spotted along the way.`,tip:`Start early to beat the heat and the crowds; reward yourself with coffee at the summit café, then walk back down.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Waterfall Gully, South Australia`},{id:`mount-lofty-summit`,name:`Mount Lofty Summit`,category:`nature`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`sunset`,`night-view`,`free`],area:`Adelaide Hills`,lat:-34.9765,lng:138.7078,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`At 727 m, the highest point of the Mount Lofty Ranges, with a lookout taking in the whole city grid, the plains and Gulf St Vincent.`,tip:`A 25-minute drive from the city; come at dusk to watch the city lights come on.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Mount Lofty`},{id:`cleland-wildlife-park`,name:`Cleland Wildlife Park`,category:`family`,tags:[`wildlife`,`koalas`,`kangaroos`,`kids`],area:`Adelaide Hills`,lat:-34.9677,lng:138.6972,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:24,rating:4,description:`A bushland park just below Mount Lofty where kangaroos, wallabies and emus roam free among visitors and you can get up close to koalas.`,tip:`Buy a bag of feed at the entrance for the kangaroos, and check the times for the koala close-up sessions.`,indoor:!1},{id:`morialta-conservation-park`,name:`Morialta Conservation Park`,category:`nature`,tags:[`hiking`,`waterfall`,`gorge`,`free`,`koalas`],area:`Morialta`,lat:-34.8964,lng:138.7028,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A rocky gorge in the foothills with trails linking three waterfalls, cliffs popular with climbers and a good chance of spotting koalas in the gums.`,tip:`The falls flow best in winter and spring; the Three Falls Grand Hike loop takes around 2.5 hours.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Morialta Conservation Park`},{id:`penfolds-magill-estate`,name:`Penfolds Magill Estate`,category:`food`,tags:[`wine`,`winery`,`tasting`,`history`],area:`Magill`,lat:-34.9172,lng:138.6755,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:3,description:`The 1844 birthplace of Penfolds and of Grange, Australia's most famous wine, with a historic cellar door and a vineyard just 8 km from the city centre.`,tip:`Book a heritage tour or tasting ahead; it is an easy alternative if you cannot fit in a full wine-region day.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Penfolds`},{id:`hahndorf`,name:`Hahndorf and the Adelaide Hills`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`german`,`village`,`wine`,`heritage`],area:`Hahndorf`,lat:-35.0292,lng:138.8095,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`Australia's oldest surviving German settlement, founded by Prussian Lutherans in 1839, its tree-lined main street full of bakeries, smallgoods shops and pubs, with cool-climate cellar doors all around.`,tip:`About 30 minutes' drive from the city. Combine with Mount Lofty and a cellar door or two, and pick up strawberries at Beerenberg Farm in season.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hahndorf, South Australia`},{id:`barossa-valley`,name:`Barossa Valley day trip`,category:`food`,tags:[`day-trip`,`wine`,`winery`,`tasting`,`iconic`],area:`Barossa Valley`,lat:-34.5244,lng:138.959,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:80,rating:5,description:`One of the world's great wine regions, an hour north-east of the city, famous for old-vine shiraz, German-heritage villages like Tanunda and grand estates such as Seppeltsfield.`,tip:`Do not drive yourself if you plan to taste properly: join a small-group tour, or book a driver. Many cellar doors now charge a tasting fee, often waived if you buy.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Barossa Valley`},{id:`mclaren-vale`,name:`McLaren Vale day trip`,category:`food`,tags:[`day-trip`,`wine`,`winery`,`beach`,`tasting`],area:`McLaren Vale`,lat:-35.219,lng:138.5433,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:70,rating:4,description:`A Mediterranean-feeling wine region 40 minutes south of the city, known for shiraz and grenache, with relaxed cellar doors between the hills and the beaches of the Fleurieu coast.`,tip:`End the day at Port Willunga beach for sunset; book tastings ahead at weekends.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`McLaren Vale, South Australia`}],foods:[{name:`Pie Floater`,description:`Adelaide's gloriously odd late-night classic: a meat pie sitting upside down in a bowl of thick green pea soup, crowned with tomato sauce.`},{name:`Yiros`,description:`Adelaide's word for the Greek gyros: shaved lamb or chicken rolled in warm pita with tomato, onion, tzatziki and often chips, a legacy of the city's big Greek community.`},{name:`King George Whiting`,description:`South Australia's most prized fish, sweet and delicate, usually served lightly battered or grilled with chips and lemon.`},{name:`Kitchener Bun`,description:`A South Australian bakery staple: a sugar-dusted doughnut split and filled with jam and cream, sometimes custard too.`},{name:`Barossa Mettwurst`,description:`A smoky, tangy cured sausage brought by German settlers to the Barossa and Hahndorf, sliced thin on platters with cheese and pickles.`},{name:`FruChocs`,description:`Adelaide's own sweet since 1948: balls of apricot and peach paste coated in milk or dark chocolate, made by local confectioner Menz.`}]},{id:`hobart`,name:`Hobart`,lat:-42.8821,lng:147.3272,timezone:`Australia/Hobart`,tagline:`Harbour town under a mountain, with MONA, markets and convict history`,description:`Australia's second-oldest capital spreads around the deep Derwent estuary beneath the bulk of kunanyi / Mount Wellington. Sandstone warehouses along Salamanca Place, a working waterfront of fish punts and the provocative MONA museum make a compact, walkable city, and Tasmania's wild coasts, convict sites and national parks are an easy day out.`,idealDays:[3,5],places:[{id:`mona-hobart`,name:`MONA (Museum of Old and New Art)`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`iconic`,`ferry`,`rainy-day`,`winery`],area:`Berriedale`,lat:-42.8124,lng:147.2607,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:5,description:`A subversive private museum dug into a riverside sandstone cliff, where ancient antiquities sit beside challenging contemporary art about sex and death; the ride up the Derwent by ferry is half the fun.`,tip:`Usually open Friday to Monday only (plus Thursdays in summer), so check before planning; book the ferry from Brooke Street Pier with your ticket.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museum of Old and New Art`},{id:`salamanca-place`,name:`Salamanca Place`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`heritage`,`sandstone`,`free`,`dining`],area:`Salamanca`,lat:-42.8873,lng:147.331,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A row of 1830s sandstone warehouses built by convicts for the whaling port, now galleries, shops, pubs and restaurants facing a plane-tree-lined square.`,tip:`Climb the convict-cut Kelly's Steps at the back to reach Battery Point.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Salamanca Place`},{id:`salamanca-market`,name:`Salamanca Market`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`market`,`iconic`,`crafts`,`local-produce`,`weekend`],area:`Salamanca`,lat:-42.8869,lng:147.33,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:5,description:`Saturdays only: around 300 stalls of Tasmanian produce, woodwork, crafts, buskers and street food fill Salamanca Place, a Hobart tradition since 1972.`,tip:`Saturday only, about 8:30am to 3pm. Come early for the best produce and fewer crowds, and try a scallop pie from a food stall.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Salamanca Market`},{id:`salamanca-arts-centre`,name:`Salamanca Arts Centre`,category:`culture`,tags:[`art`,`galleries`,`design`,`rainy-day`,`free`],area:`Salamanca`,lat:-42.8866,lng:147.3309,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Seven old warehouses turned into a creative hub of small galleries, artists' studios, design shops and a little theatre.`,tip:`A good wet-weather browse, with Tasmanian-made gifts in the design shops.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Salamanca Arts Centre`},{id:`knopwoods-retreat`,name:`Knopwood's Retreat`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`pub`,`heritage`,`night`,`local`],area:`Salamanca`,lat:-42.8859,lng:147.3297,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:3,description:`A creaky old sandstone pub at the end of Salamanca Place, where Friday-evening crowds spill out onto the footpath with pints in hand.`,tip:`Friday after work is the classic time; arrive early for a seat by the fire in winter.`,indoor:!0},{id:`battery-point`,name:`Battery Point and Arthur Circus`,category:`culture`,tags:[`heritage`,`cottages`,`walk`,`free`,`photo-spot`],area:`Battery Point`,lat:-42.8906,lng:147.3315,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Hobart's old maritime quarter of narrow lanes and Georgian cottages, centred on Arthur Circus, a ring of tiny 1840s houses around a village green.`,tip:`Walk up Kelly's Steps from Salamanca, loop through Arthur Circus and stop for a pie at a Hampden Road bakery.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Battery Point, Tasmania`},{id:`kunanyi-mount-wellington`,name:`kunanyi / Mount Wellington summit`,localName:`kunanyi`,category:`nature`,tags:[`iconic`,`viewpoint`,`mountain`,`sunset`,`free`],area:`Mount Wellington`,lat:-42.8959,lng:147.2362,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The 1,271 m mountain that looms over the city, with a summit boardwalk and glassed-in lookout over Hobart, the Derwent and much of southern Tasmania.`,tip:`Take warm layers even in summer, as it can snow at the top. Without a car, use the Explorer bus; the road sometimes closes for ice.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Mount Wellington (Tasmania)`},{id:`organ-pipes-walk`,name:`Organ Pipes track`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`hiking`,`mountain`,`cliffs`,`free`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Mount Wellington`,lat:-42.8919,lng:147.2449,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A rocky mountain trail beneath the towering dolerite columns of the Organ Pipes, with views over the city all the way.`,tip:`Start from The Chalet on Pinnacle Road; it is rough underfoot, so wear proper shoes.`,indoor:!1},{id:`tasmanian-museum-and-art-gallery`,name:`Tasmanian Museum and Art Gallery (TMAG)`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`aboriginal-culture`,`art`,`free`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`Waterfront`,lat:-42.8818,lng:147.3315,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A free museum set around the colony's oldest buildings, covering palawa Aboriginal culture, convict history, colonial art, the extinct thylacine and Antarctica.`,tip:`Do not miss the thylacine gallery; it is closed on Mondays outside summer, so check the hours.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Tasmanian Museum and Art Gallery`},{id:`constitution-dock-fish-punts`,name:`Constitution Dock fish punts`,category:`food`,tags:[`seafood`,`waterfront`,`fish-and-chips`,`local`],area:`Waterfront`,lat:-42.8833,lng:147.3319,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:4,description:`Floating fish-and-chip punts moored in the dock where the Sydney to Hobart yachts finish, frying local flathead, scallops and blue grenadier.`,tip:`Eat on the dockside benches, and keep an eye on the seagulls.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Constitution Dock`},{id:`sullivans-cove-waterfront`,name:`Sullivans Cove waterfront`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`waterfront`,`walk`,`free`,`night-view`,`harbour`],area:`Waterfront`,lat:-42.8844,lng:147.3342,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The site of Hobart's 1804 settlement, now a harbourside promenade linking Franklin Wharf, Brooke Street Pier and the old docks, with the mountain as a backdrop.`,tip:`Walk it at dusk, when the mountain glows and the waterfront restaurants light up.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Sullivans Cove`},{id:`mawsons-huts-replica-museum`,name:`Mawson's Huts Replica Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`antarctica`,`history`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`Waterfront`,lat:-42.8831,lng:147.3338,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`An exact replica of the huts Douglas Mawson's expedition built in Antarctica in 1911, kitted out with bunks, stores and original artefacts, near the wharf the expedition sailed from.`,tip:`Takes under an hour; ticket money supports conservation of the real huts in Antarctica.`,indoor:!0},{id:`maritime-museum-of-tasmania`,name:`Maritime Museum of Tasmania`,category:`museum`,tags:[`ships`,`history`,`whaling`,`rainy-day`],area:`Waterfront`,lat:-42.883,lng:147.3308,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`A small museum in the Carnegie Building telling the story of Tasmania's whalers, explorers, shipwrecks and Antarctic voyages.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Maritime Museum of Tasmania`},{id:`theatre-royal-hobart`,name:`Theatre Royal`,category:`culture`,tags:[`theatre`,`heritage`,`night`,`rainy-day`],area:`CBD`,lat:-42.8807,lng:147.3317,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:55,rating:3,description:`Australia's oldest continuously operating theatre, opened in 1837, with a jewel-box auditorium hosting plays, music and comedy.`,tip:`Check what is on before you go; even a modest show is worth it to sit in the historic auditorium.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Theatre Royal, Hobart`},{id:`st-davids-cathedral-hobart`,name:`St David's Cathedral`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`architecture`,`free`,`gothic-revival`],area:`CBD`,lat:-42.8829,lng:147.3279,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:2,description:`Hobart's Anglican cathedral, a sandstone Gothic Revival church with fine woodwork and old regimental colours inside.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`St David's Cathedral, Hobart`},{id:`farm-gate-market`,name:`Farm Gate Market`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`local-produce`,`weekend`,`breakfast`],area:`CBD`,lat:-42.8804,lng:147.3256,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`A Sunday growers' market on Bathurst Street where Tasmanian farmers, bakers, cheesemakers and distillers sell straight to locals.`,tip:`Sundays only, from about 8:30am to 1pm; breakfast at the stalls is part of the ritual.`,indoor:!1},{id:`penitentiary-chapel-historic-site`,name:`Hobart Penitentiary (Penitentiary Chapel Historic Site)`,category:`museum`,tags:[`convict`,`history`,`ghost-tour`,`heritage`],area:`CBD`,lat:-42.8796,lng:147.3297,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:23,rating:3,description:`Hobart's 1830s convict prison chapel, with underground tunnels, solitary cells, courtrooms and gallows shown on guided tours by the National Trust.`,tip:`Book a guided tour, or the lantern-lit ghost tour after dark; it has steep, narrow stairs.`,indoor:!0},{id:`state-cinema-hobart`,name:`State Cinema`,category:`culture`,tags:[`cinema`,`art-house`,`rooftop`,`night`,`rainy-day`],area:`North Hobart`,lat:-42.8698,lng:147.3165,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:15,rating:3,description:`A much-loved independent cinema in a 1913 picture house, showing art-house and new releases, with a rooftop screen and bar.`,tip:`Grab dinner on the North Hobart strip first; there is a good bookshop next door too.`,indoor:!0},{id:`north-hobart-dining`,name:`Elizabeth Street, North Hobart`,category:`food`,tags:[`dining`,`restaurants`,`night`,`local`],area:`North Hobart`,lat:-42.8705,lng:147.317,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:3,description:`Locals' restaurant row, a strip of Elizabeth Street crowded with Thai, Indian, Italian and Japanese restaurants, wine bars and pubs.`,tip:`A 20-minute walk or short bus ride up from the city; good for an easy weeknight dinner.`,indoor:!1},{id:`royal-tasmanian-botanical-gardens`,name:`Royal Tasmanian Botanical Gardens`,category:`nature`,tags:[`garden`,`free`,`park`,`kids`],area:`Queens Domain`,lat:-42.8646,lng:147.3297,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Gardens founded in 1818 on the Queens Domain, with a Japanese garden, a subantarctic plant house that recreates Macquarie Island, and convict-built walls.`,tip:`Free entry; the subantarctic plant house is a fun, chilly surprise on a hot day.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Royal Tasmanian Botanical Gardens`},{id:`cascade-brewery`,name:`Cascade Brewery`,category:`food`,tags:[`beer`,`brewery-tour`,`heritage`,`gardens`],area:`South Hobart`,lat:-42.8964,lng:147.2953,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:3,description:`Australia's oldest operating brewery, founded in 1824, its gothic stone facade set against the forested foot of the mountain, with tours, tastings and a garden bar.`,tip:`Book a brewery tour ahead (16+, closed shoes required) or just have a paddle in the beer garden.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Cascade Brewery`},{id:`cascades-female-factory`,name:`Cascades Female Factory Historic Site`,category:`museum`,tags:[`convict`,`history`,`unesco`,`heritage`],area:`South Hobart`,lat:-42.8938,lng:147.3007,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:3,description:`Part of the World Heritage-listed Australian Convict Sites, this former women's prison tells the hard stories of thousands of convict women and their children.`,tip:`Join the guided tour or the short dramatised "Her Story" performance to bring the empty yards to life.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Cascades Female Factory`},{id:`hobart-rivulet-track`,name:`Hobart Rivulet track`,category:`nature`,tags:[`walk`,`free`,`creek`,`hidden-gem`],area:`South Hobart`,lat:-42.8882,lng:147.3148,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A gentle creekside path from the edge of the CBD up to the Female Factory and Cascade Brewery, where platypus are sometimes spotted.`,tip:`Walk up to the brewery and catch a bus back; platypus are most likely early morning or at dusk.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hobart Rivulet`},{id:`mount-nelson-signal-station`,name:`Mount Nelson Signal Station`,category:`nature`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`history`,`free`,`cafe`],area:`Mount Nelson`,lat:-42.9215,lng:147.3191,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`An 1811 semaphore station with a sweeping view down the Derwent to the sea, and a café in the old signalman's cottage.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Mount Nelson Signal Station`},{id:`wrest-point`,name:`Wrest Point`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`casino`,`night-view`,`revolving-restaurant`,`night`],area:`Sandy Bay`,lat:-42.9023,lng:147.3345,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:55,rating:2,description:`Australia's first legal casino, opened in 1973 in a riverside tower, topped by a revolving restaurant with panoramic night views.`,tip:`Even if you do not gamble, a drink or dinner up top is a fun way to see the city lights.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Wrest Point Hotel Casino`},{id:`derwent-sea-kayaking`,name:`Sea kayaking on the Derwent`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`kayak`,`water`,`guided-tour`,`harbour`],area:`Sandy Bay`,lat:-42.8953,lng:147.3376,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:70,rating:3,description:`Guided paddles from Sandy Bay along the river and into the docks, seeing the waterfront and mountain from water level.`,tip:`Tours run daily in summer but only some days in winter; book ahead and expect a cold-water briefing.`,indoor:!1},{id:`kingston-beach`,name:`Kingston Beach`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`beach`,`free`,`kids`,`walk`],area:`Kingston Beach`,lat:-42.9764,lng:147.3221,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:2,description:`A sheltered sandy beach 15 minutes south of the city, with a seaside café strip and walks along the river.`,tip:`The water is chilly year-round; come for a walk and coffee more than a swim.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Kingston Beach`},{id:`gasp-glenorchy`,name:`GASP (Glenorchy Art and Sculpture Park)`,category:`culture`,tags:[`sculpture`,`free`,`walk`,`architecture`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Glenorchy`,lat:-42.8192,lng:147.2764,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:2,description:`A striking boardwalk and pavilion snaking around Elwick Bay, dotted with sculpture and views across the Derwent, a short hop from MONA.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Glenorchy Art and Sculpture Park`},{id:`bonorong-wildlife-sanctuary`,name:`Bonorong Wildlife Sanctuary`,category:`family`,tags:[`wildlife`,`tasmanian-devils`,`kangaroos`,`kids`],area:`Brighton`,lat:-42.7065,lng:147.244,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`A rescue sanctuary 30 minutes north of the city where you can hand-feed free-roaming kangaroos and meet Tasmanian devils, wombats and quolls.`,tip:`Join one of the free guided tours through the day; night tours are worth booking to see nocturnal animals awake.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Bonorong Wildlife Sanctuary`},{id:`richmond-tasmania`,name:`Richmond village and bridge`,category:`culture`,tags:[`heritage`,`village`,`convict`,`bridge`,`wine`],area:`Richmond`,lat:-42.7347,lng:147.4404,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`A Georgian village 25 minutes from Hobart, home to Australia's oldest bridge (1823), the oldest surviving gaol and Coal River Valley cellar doors.`,tip:`Combine with Bonorong for an easy half-day; the bridge is prettiest in morning light.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Richmond, Tasmania`},{id:`port-arthur`,name:`Port Arthur Historic Site`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`day-trip`,`convict`,`unesco`,`iconic`,`history`],area:`Port Arthur`,lat:-43.1481,lng:147.8509,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:5,description:`Australia's most famous convict site, the haunting ruins of an 1830s penal settlement on a green bay, with a harbour cruise to the Isle of the Dead included.`,tip:`About 90 minutes' drive; stop at Eaglehawk Neck's Tessellated Pavement and Tasman Arch on the way. Tickets are valid for two days.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Port Arthur, Tasmania`},{id:`bruny-island`,name:`Bruny Island day trip`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`island`,`wildlife`,`oysters`,`coast`],area:`Bruny Island`,lat:-43.2715,lng:147.3556,durationHours:9,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:90,rating:4,description:`A wild island across a short car ferry from Kettering, known for The Neck lookout, towering sea cliffs, white wallabies, oysters, cheese and whisky.`,tip:`The ferry fills up in summer, so book ahead; the 3-hour wilderness boat cruise from Adventure Bay is a highlight.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Bruny Island`},{id:`mount-field-national-park`,name:`Mount Field National Park`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`waterfall`,`tall-trees`,`hiking`],area:`Mount Field`,lat:-42.6824,lng:146.7154,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`Tasmania's first national park, an hour and a quarter from Hobart, where an easy walk through tree ferns leads to tiered Russell Falls and on past some of the world's tallest flowering trees.`,tip:`A Parks pass is required per vehicle. Add the Three Falls circuit, and look for glow-worms at Russell Falls after dark.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Mount Field National Park`}],foods:[{name:`Scallop Pie`,description:`Tasmania's signature pie: plump local scallops in a mild yellow curry sauce under flaky pastry, sold at bakeries and markets.`},{name:`Tasmanian Oysters`,description:`Plump, briny Pacific oysters from the cold waters of Bruny Island, Pittwater and the east coast, usually eaten raw with lemon.`},{name:`Flathead and Chips`,description:`The classic Hobart fish supper: sweet, flaky local flathead in batter with chips, best from a waterfront fish punt.`},{name:`Tasmanian Salmon`,description:`Atlantic salmon farmed in Tasmania's cold southern waters, served smoked, cured, raw or pan-fried with crispy skin.`},{name:`Leatherwood Honey`,description:`A distinctive, spicy-floral honey made only from the flowers of the leatherwood tree in Tasmania's western rainforests.`},{name:`Tasmanian Whisky`,description:`Award-winning single malts from a wave of small island distilleries, sipped neat in waterfront whisky bars.`}]}]};export{e as australia};